export const LICHEN_DOCTRINE = "HOW TO USE WHAT FOLLOWS\n\nThis is Lichen's own engineering documentation. It is given to you so your\nanswers are TRUE and current, not so you can recite it.\n\n- TRANSLATE, never quote. A member asking why they can't find someone should\n  hear \"they've set themselves unfindable\", never \"profiles.findable\" or the\n  name of a policy, table, migration or edge function.\n- The DOCTRINE is the valuable part, not the schema. Why there are no counts.\n  Why unknown is never yes. Why a confused member is a design bug, not a user\n  error. That reasoning is what makes an answer sound like Lichen.\n- Anything marked as vision, open, planned or not-yet-built DOES NOT EXIST.\n  Never describe it as something a member can use today.\n- If the documentation contradicts what a member is seeing, believe the\n  member and say you're not sure. The docs describe intent; their screen is\n  the fact.\n\n===== CLAUDE.md — The project brain: how Lichen works and WHY it was built this way. =====\n\n# Lichen — PWA project guide\n\nLichen is a holistic-healing nonprofit + conscious-economy platform. This repo\n(`lichenhealth/mobilewebapp`, package `lichen-pwa`) is the member-facing PWA.\nThe founder is non-technical; explain reasoning briefly and prefer small,\nreviewable changes. Keep Plan Mode on for anything touching the database or auth.\n\nFor the dated, PR-by-PR story of how any of this got built — the \"why\" behind\na non-obvious decision — see [`docs/HISTORY.md`](docs/HISTORY.md). This file\nis the current-state reference only.\n\n## Stack & deploy\n- React 18 + Vite + TypeScript. Build: `tsc -b && vite build` (it type-checks — always run before considering a change done, and fix all errors; the project builds clean).\n- No package-lock; Vercel runs `npm install`. Vercel auto-deploys `main` on push.\n- Backend: Supabase (project `mjqnaevertyzgjlpwynr`). Anon key is hardcoded in `src/lib/supabase.ts` (public by design; RLS protects data).\n- DB schema is version-controlled in `supabase/migrations/00000000000000_init.sql` — a `pg_dump --schema-only --schema=public` baseline plus a manually-appended `auth.users` signup trigger. It's a record/backup, not auto-applied — the live schema is edited in the Supabase dashboard and this file can drift; refresh it after DB changes. Supabase CLI is linked (`supabase/config.toml`); `pg_dump` lives at `/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin/pg_dump` (no Docker). `supabase db dump`/`db pull` need Docker, which isn't installed — use the direct `pg_dump` against the session pooler instead.\n- Migrations can run directly: `worker/migrate.sh <file>` applies a migration via `psql` (`/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin/psql`) using `SUPABASE_DB_URL` from the gitignored `worker/.env` (session-pooler URI, founder-supplied, never passes through chat). Runs as one transaction (`ON_ERROR_STOP` + `psql -1`) — a failure rolls back cleanly. Routine additive migrations can run directly and get reported after; anything destructive (dropping a column, deleting rows, rewriting existing data) needs the founder's explicit yes first.\n\n### Domains & email\n- `lichen.health` **is the app** — canonical origin (`APP_ORIGIN` in `src/lib/customDomain.ts`, `APP_URL` edge secret). `lichen.healthcare` (+www, and www.lichen.health) 308-redirects every path to the same path on `lichen.health` via `vercel.json` host-matched rules. ⚠ `/:path*` does **not** match the bare root on host rules — explicit `source: \"/\"` rules exist for each host; keep both when adding a new host.\n- DNS: `lichen.health` stays on **Wix** nameservers (A record → Vercel). **Google-Workspace MX for `connect@lichen.health` lives there — never touch.** Transactional email still sends **from** `lichen.healthcare` (Resend MX; deliberate, invisible to members).\n- Signed-out `/` on `lichen.health` serves the static Astro marketing homepage (`public/welcome/` — filesystem-first, shadows the SPA rewrite; bounces to `/home` via a localStorage auth-token check for signed-in browsers). `/get-involved`, `/founders-circle`, `/project/*` also ship static. The app itself keeps a richer in-app version of `/about`; `/blog /resources /mission /ourstory` etc. redirect to it in `App.tsx`. PWA manifest `start_url` = `/home` (installed apps skip the marketing shell).\n- The old marketing site's long-form essay/reading-list import (11 founding essays + 6 reading lists, `'The Lichen essays'` / `'The Lichen bookshelf'` collections) was removed from Library 2026-08-10 — founder call, replacing it with better-curated content; full content archived to `archive/lichen_essays_and_bookshelf_backup_2026-08-10.json` before deletion. Anon users can still read public posts + published collections generally (signed-out browsing is deliberate — the growth loop); this just isn't what carries that anymore.\n- To edit a static marketing page: edit the `lichenhealth/lichen-health` repo (Astro) → `npm run build` → copy the built page dirs + `_astro` into this repo's `public/` (re-inject the `welcome/index.html` auth-bounce script — it's hand-patched, not part of the Astro build) → push **both** repos. ⚠ Never `rsync --delete` the shared `public/_astro/` unless EVERY page dir ships in the same copy — hashed assets referenced by pages you didn't re-copy get deleted out from under them (it took `/welcome`'s stylesheet on 2026-08-13; restored from git). Copy `_astro` additively, or verify every `public/*/index.html`'s `/_astro/` references still resolve before pushing.\n\n### Local verification with a test account\nThere's one live Supabase project (no separate staging), so \"local\" verification means the local Vite dev server against the real database, signed in as a dedicated, low-stakes account (`galyn+claudetest@lichen.health`, profile name \"Claude Test\", gifted a Community subscription) — never the founder's real one. Claude does not type a password into a login form or call `signInWithPassword` itself, even for this throwaway account — that's a hard rule, not a preference.\n\n**Getting a session (no founder involvement needed):** `worker/mint-test-session.sh [email]` mints a fresh session server-side via Supabase's Admin Auth API (`generate_link` → `verify`) using the service-role key already in `worker/.env`, and writes it to `worker/test-session.json` (gitignored — same trust boundary as `worker/.env`). Standing Bash permission rule already covers running it, no approval prompt. Claude then injects the contents into the Browser-pane preview via `localStorage.setItem('sb-mjqnaevertyzgjlpwynr-auth-token', <contents>)` + reload.\n\nFallback (only if the account doesn't exist yet, or the service-role key isn't available): the founder signs into the account once in their own browser, opens devtools → Application → Local Storage, and copies the `sb-mjqnaevertyzgjlpwynr-auth-token` value into `worker/test-session.json` by hand.\n\n**Standing protocol (founder, 2026-08-15): SWEEP the widths, don't spot-check two.** Every UI change is reviewed by resizing the Browser pane ACROSS the range — ~360 · 700 · 1024 · 1440 at minimum — and watching it adapt, not just at the mobile and desktop defaults. What to assert at each stop: no horizontal overflow (`documentElement.scrollWidth > clientWidth`), rows wrap rather than clip, and elements that should hug an edge still do. ⚠ Between ~430 and 1024 the whole `.app-shell` is a CENTERED phone-width column (`--app-max: 430px`) — an element measured far from the viewport's left edge there may be correctly hugging its column; measure against the shell, not the window. ⚠ A flex CHILD stretches full-width by default: `display: inline-flex` alone won't make a chip hug left inside these flex-column pages — it needs `align-self: flex-start` (this is what made ScopeBack span the page).\n\n**Standing protocol (founder, 2026-08-09): test before declaring UI work done.** For any UI/frontend push, sign in as the test account and actually click through the changed flow at both mobile and desktop widths in the Browser pane — not just a code read or a single screenshot — before reporting complete. Fix whatever's found, re-verify, then report. This is load-bearing, not optional polish; it's already caught real bugs (a popover-overlap and an off-screen-clipping bug) that a code read alone missed.\n\n## Sessions — why \"signed in but signed out\" kept happening\nRoot-caused 2026-08-14 (reproduced end to end, not guessed). Two different\nfailures wore the same face:\n- **A rejected refresh** (server says the token is dead — revocation, rotation\n  reuse, an explicit sign-out elsewhere) CLEARS storage. That is a real sign\n  out; showing the Sign-in pill is correct.\n- **A failed refresh** (network unreachable: asleep laptop, flapping wifi, a\n  power cut) leaves the token INTACT in storage, but supabase-js's in-memory\n  session goes null and **never returns on its own** — auto-refresh only ticks\n  for a session it still holds. The app then rendered full signed-out chrome\n  (Sign in pill, no sidebar) to a member whose session was perfectly valid, so\n  they signed in again. One badly-timed refresh was enough.\nThe fix is re-hydration + honesty, in `AuthProvider.tsx`: `storedSession()`\n(`src/lib/supabase.ts`, which also now pins `storageKey` explicitly) tells\n\"signed out\" from \"temporarily unreachable\"; a **watchdog** (on `online`, on\ntab-visible, and every 8s while there's no session) re-adopts the stored\nsession via `setSession()` — `refreshSession()` is wrong here, the client has\nnothing in memory to refresh. While the gap lasts the app says\n**\"Reconnecting…\"**, keeps the sidebar, and never sends anyone to /login.\n⚠ Never gate recovery on having NOTICED the gap (an auth event may never\nfire); watch the condition itself. ⚠ Verified live: unreachable-auth boot →\nReconnecting + token preserved; network back → signed in again in ~1.2s with\nno reload; genuinely signed out → Sign in, as it should be.\n\n## Conventions\n- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (peach accent `--peach`, blue `--blue` for admin/stewardship affordances, green `--green` for availability/free, bone canvas, Archivo body, display serif). Reuse token vars; match existing BEM-ish class names (`.onb__`, `.prof__`, `.cat__`, `.adminc__`, `.conv-row`, `.thread__`).\n- Logo: `src/components/LichenMark.tsx`. Icons: `src/components/Icon.tsx` (`<Icon name=... size=... />`; top-bar section marks force 1.2px hairline strokes via `vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke` — native strokeWidths are tuned for small sizes).\n- Avoid the word \"spaces\" in member-facing UI when you mean the ENTITIES — say organizations / communities / groups / places. Bookable **resources** are \"Bookable areas & things\" (founder 2026-08-11) — a stall or an arena isn't a room, and \"areas\" keeps \"spaces\" reserved for the entities. The DB column stays `resources.kind = room|thing`; only the labels changed.\n- Supabase embeds: when a table has >1 FK to another, disambiguate with the explicit hint, e.g. `profiles!subscriptions_profile_id_fkey(full_name)`. SELF-referencing FKs (`spaces.parent_space_id`): do **not** embed at all — the FK-NAME hint fails outright and the COLUMN hint `spaces!parent_space_id(...)` parses but resolves to the CHILDREN direction (an array). Fetch the parent row explicitly by `parent_space_id` instead (see `spacesApi` `loadSpaceProfile`/`listSpacesByKind`).\n- React hooks must ALL sit above any early return (`if (loading) return …`). A hook added below one crashes the whole app to a blank page when the data arrives (\"Rendered more hooks…\").\n- New enum values can't be USED in the same migration that adds them — add in a separate step that's committed first.\n- Only 3 columns use real Postgres enums (`account_capability`, `space_kind`, `space_member_role`). Other \"enum-like\" fields (care `status`, subscription `tier`/`source`, category `domain`, suggestion `status`) are actually `text` columns with CHECK constraints — to add a value, change the CHECK, not an enum type.\n- RLS policies must never reference each other in a cycle (42P17 recursion) — route through a `SECURITY DEFINER` helper instead (`is_chat_member()`, `is_event_attendee()`, `owns_reminder()`, `is_space_admin()` are the existing examples; reuse the pattern for any new two-tables-reference-each-other case — including hand-rolled duplicates of an existing helper, which sit on the same latent-cycle shape even before they've actually recursed).\n- Migrations pasted through the Supabase dashboard need a **named** dollar-quote tag (`$func$`, not `$$`) — the dashboard's paste can mangle a bare `$$` into `$` (42601).\n- `.app-shell` must stay `overflow-x: clip`, never `hidden` — `hidden` silently kills `position: sticky` app-wide.\n- `.h-scroll`'s own 12px gap beats a row's own `gap` — new horizontally-scrolling rows need a double-class selector (`.icon-row.h-scroll` etc.) to override it.\n- `tokens.css`'s `--wall-gutter` is applied globally via `.scroll-view`'s `padding-inline` — a mandatory minimum side indent even when a section forgets its own padding. Full-bleed screens (chat thread, auth, maps, about, guest pages) opt out via an explicit inline `padding: 0` in `App.tsx`.\n- `\\u` escapes do not process inside JSX attribute strings — write the literal character in placeholder text, not the escape sequence.\n- A recurring class of bug: a shared row's own back-chip/back-button styling loses an import-order specificity tie against a page-specific override. Fix with a compound selector (e.g. `.cmp__back.postp__back`), never a bare rule.\n- **Scoped sections are the platform through a filter** (founder 2026-08-11) and must read as themselves even at zero. Shared parts (the `ScopeEscape` header chip was RETIRED 2026-08-13 — founder: with the way out living where the content should be, the extra button was redundant and made the UI busy): `ScopeEmpty` says \"No Library content from Countryman Stables yet!\" with a \"Visit the Lichen Library\" link (founder's wording) rather than a generic blank; and `TopBar` overlays the scoping entity's avatar on the section logo (`.top-bar__scope-badge`, the founder's preferred design solve over renaming the page) so you can see whose Library/Marketplace you're in. **A thin shelf gets the same pointer as a bare one** (founder 2026-08-13): `ScopeMore` sits UNDER the results when a scoped section has fewer than `FEW_RESULTS` (5) — \"That's all the one thing Pine Valley Grange has in Marketplace so far\" + a way to the whole section — never replacing what's there, unlike `ScopeEmpty` at zero. Wired in `Marketplace.tsx` + `AreaFeed.tsx` (courses/library/art/work/food/travel) + **`Events.tsx`** (which understood `?space=` all along but never got the shared pattern) and My-celium's empty web. ⚠ **Scope comes from the URL (`?space=`/`?member=`), never from acting-as** (founder 2026-08-13, asked and answered): reaching Marketplace from the icon row while wearing an org's hat is Lichen's Marketplace, deliberately — \"I want to be able to participate in the lichen marketplace as countryman stables... I'm always a participant, even if i'm an org\". So the ACTIONS carry the hat instead: Compose already authors as the space (`author_space_id`, with a \"Posting as\" banner), Current-cy already treats a space as a first-class party, and Marketplace now passes `asSpace` to `setRecommend` (⚠ read the state back with `recommendKey(...asSpace)` — the key appends `@<spaceId>`, so the bare key leaves the thumb dark). STILL PERSONAL: trust (a space has no shield, by doctrine) and messaging (`chat_members` has no space column). **Buying works through the EXCHANGE flow** (`exchanges` table, request → accept → both-say-done → Current moves; `ExchangePanel` on PostPage) — and since 2026-08-13 a space can be the BUYER (`exchanges.buyer_space_id`; `buyer_id` still records which admin acted, the truster_id pattern) and a space seller is paid INTO its treasury (completion used to credit the human who posted the space's listing — the treasury was bypassed on its own sales). The not_self rule relaxes only when a space is the real buyer (\"the barn buys its admin's saddle\"); a treasury purchase is admin-gated, not guardian-gated, but a minor SELLER still needs a guardian's yes. `request_exchange` gained `p_as_space` (old 4-arg dropped — one PostgREST candidate); `complete_exchange` debits/credits the PARTIES (space or person, either side), takes the same advisory-lock keyspace as `send_currentcy`, and bells a receiving treasury's admins; the frozen price now takes the FIRST number in the text (the old strip-non-numerics turned \"sliding $10–$25\" into **1025 Current**). `send_currentcy` also bells a space recipient's admins now. ⚠ `lichen.actingAs.<uid>` in localStorage stores a BARE space/being id, not JSON — inject accordingly when testing. `possessive()` in `src/lib/names.ts` gives \"Countryman Stables'\", not \"Stables's\".\n- `loadFeed()` is the shared source for Events/Marketplace/AreaFeed/Maps/search — any filter added there needs to be **opt-in** (a flag like `{ river: true }`), not applied by default, or it silently drops posts from every other surface that calls it. Same pattern: Compose's \"Skip the feed\" writes `details.quiet`, honored only where `river: true` is passed.\n- Consent bubbles (`ConsentBubble.tsx`) are the pattern for a setting that needs in-context explanation (presence, findability): anchored to the control it governs, an \"Edit `<setting>`\" door, only one visible at a time, seen-state tracked per **member** via `member_prompts` (not per device — a new phone isn't a changed mind, so don't re-prompt on it).\n- The Home **Directory** (`Directory.tsx`, `/directory`) lists EVERYONE since 2026-08-14: members first (trust shield), then **Stewarded members** (non-person `profiles.kind` rows — plant/animal/place/element/collective, each with a steward who answers for it; founder 2026-08-14 chose the literal name over a prettier one, the same instinct that retired \"awake\"), then findable Organizations/Communities/Groups/Places (`.dir__section` headers, My-celium's ordering) — beings and spaces carry the recommend thumb, never a shield (trust is person-to-person). Search spans all of it. `MemberRow.tsx` is the one shared row for every member/space listing (Home Directory, My-celium's web, a space's Members tab) — avatar, shield-or-thumb (person→trust, space→recommend), weave mark, labeled Message door. `chatApi.ts` exports `CLAUDE_PROFILE_ID` (the single source — don't re-inline the UUID), `sortClaudeFirst()`, and `hasDirectChatWith()` (a read-only existence check on `chats.direct_key`, unlike `ensureDirectChat` which creates the row). Claude's avatar look (Si-blue circle, brain glyph) lives in `public/claude-avatar.svg`, referenced by `profiles.avatar_url` — recolor by editing that file, not in code.\n- Desktop responsiveness (`@media (min-width: 1024px)`, matching the app-shell's own sidebar breakpoint) was historically added screen-by-screen, not systematically — a 2026-08-09/10 sweep applied two reusable idioms uniformly: row/tile lists go `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(Npx,1fr))` (`ListingTile.css`'s `.tile-grid` is the original), FeedCard stacks (Home/My-celium/AreaFeed's feed view/Saved) use the same idiom at `minmax(360px,1fr)`. `.prof` (shared by `Profile.tsx` and `SpaceProfile.tsx`) was hard-capped at the literal mobile width (`--app-max`, 430px) even inside the desktop column — fixed via a `SpaceProfile`-only `is-space` modifier class widening to 720px, leaving `Profile.tsx`'s genuinely-narrow settings page untouched. **Row-grid gotcha**: `MemberRow`'s icon+Message-button chrome alone eats ~172px, so a `minmax` narrower than ~400px truncates real names to a few px — checked only via computed-style JS the first time, which confirmed the CSS rule applied but not that the sparse test account's data was too thin to expose it; verify row grids against an account with real density, not just the test account.\n- Doors vs. lenses (founder 2026-08-08, Marketplace; extended to Events 2026-08-10): constant tools (Search, Post, the assistant, Lichen's entrust door) are icon-only circles (`.mkt__action`/`.evt__action`, no caption) — \"a circle is something you open.\" Type/mode filters (Marketplace's gift/trade/rent/etc., Events' Free/Trade/Paid) render as text+icon signal chips (`.mkt__lens`/`.evt__lens`, no circle, a check when on) — \"text with a check is something that's on.\" Marketplace splits doors and lenses onto two lines — and since 2026-08-13 **Lend + Borrow share one \"Lending\" lens** (founder: \"2 sides of the same coin\", reversing the 2026-07-17 split; DB modes stay separate — Compose still authors lend vs borrow distinctly, the merge is filter-only, `CHIP_MODES.lend = ['lend','borrow']`). The lens row also uses `ScrollHintRow`'s new **`fade` mode**: the hide-until-whole rule was written for 48px icon circles, where a hidden item's leftover layout box reads as breathing room — on a text-chip row it left an 85–120px HOLE before the chevron (the founder's circled \"empty space\" was a hidden chip's box, via `visibility: hidden`). Fade mode never hides; a cut chip tapers under a gradient to the page canvas instead. Icon rows keep hide mode — pass `fade` only for text-chip rows; Events shares one row (only 3 modes fit fine) — same vocabulary, row count follows how many filters there are, not a fixed rule. Platform-wide tab font-weight is 300 base / ~400 active (`.evt__navtab`, `.mkt__tab`, `.conc__tab`, `.evp__tab`) — `PublicPage.css`'s `.ppage__nav-link` (About/Services/etc. template tabs on member and space profiles) and `FilterRow.css`'s active state were bolder outliers (600), fixed to match.\n- Chat now has a desktop split-view: `Chat.tsx` keeps `ChatConversation` (the self-contained conversation component `ChatThread` and Concierge's care tab already reuse) inline in a `.chat__thread-pane` beside the inbox list at ≥1024px, instead of navigating to the mobile full-page `/chat/:id` (`ChatThread.tsx`) — that route/behavior is untouched below 1024px. Selection is `?open=<id>` on `/chat` (linkable/refreshable), set via `openChat()`'s desktop branch; the pane's sticky offset is `calc(var(--top-h) + var(--s-6))` to clear the topbar exactly. `ChatConversation`'s own `onBack` closes the pane back to full-width list.\n\n## Data model (all RLS-enabled)\n\n### Identity & profiles\n- `profiles` (id→auth.users; `full_name` [kept in sync from `first_name`/`last_name` by trigger `compose_full_name` — never write `full_name` client-side], `headline`, `bio`, `email`/`phone` [**not** in the column-scoped SELECT grant — owner reads via session/`my_phone()`, others never see them directly; care team reads phone via `on_call_roster()`], `onboarded`, `is_admin`, `identity_tags` text[] [public], `pronouns` [optional free text ≤40 chars, public, NULL = they/them — the assistant is told never to infer them from a name], `home_location`/`home_lat`/`home_lng`/`home_area` [not granted — owner via `my_home()`, viewers via `mappable_members()`], `presence_visible`/`presence_lit_until`/`presence_always_present`, `timezone`, `findable` [default true], `assistant_readable` [default true], `page` jsonb [public-page template content], `contact` jsonb, `public_page` bool [default **false** for people], `handle`). Trigger creates a profile on signup. `profile_locations` (2026-08-11) — a member's **Goods & Services addresses** (label + address + optional pin), as many as needed; deliberately member-visible RLS (their point is being found), unlike home's hidden-by-default `location_shares` ladder. Both managed in Profile's \"Location\" accordion section (`HomeLocationSection.tsx`, content-only — Profile supplies the CollapsibleSection chrome). Per-address `show_on_maps`/`show_on_profile` booleans (default true, instant-apply checkboxes under each row): pinned addresses ride Maps' **Places** layer (`loadBizLocationPins()` → `biz:` markers in `MapView.tsx`, popup → View member), and show-on-profile addresses render as extra Practical rows on the member's public page (`loadProfileBizLocations()` → `PublicPage`'s `bizLocations` prop via `MemberProfile.tsx` — also widens `hasContact`, so an address alone summons the Contact tab).\n- `can_see_profile()` gates profile reads (replaced a blanket `USING (true)`): visible if `findable=true`, OR you share a space/chat/care-team/web edge with them, OR you're reading one of their public posts (a feed has to be able to name its author). Because that last arm can't be replicated in a plain client query, Directory/people-search/type-aheads additionally filter `findable` themselves.\n- `profile_capabilities` (service_provider / goods_provider). `financial_positions` (pk profile_id; income_band CHECK, household_size, circumstances; RLS = owner-all + active care-team SELECT-only — never a score, never shown to anyone else).\n- `categories` (3 domains: good / service / place; text slug id, name, sort, `section` healing|everyday) + `profile_categories`. Member-suggested via `category_suggestions` + admin RPCs `approve_category_suggestion()` / `reject_category_suggestion()`.\n\n### Spaces & membership\n- `spaces` (kind enum organization|community|group|place; `created_by`; `parent_space_id` — groups nest under communities/orgs, nullable = standalone; `handle` — routes `/:handle`; `lat`/`lng`; `contact`/`page` jsonb; `public_page` [default true for org/place, false for community/group — enforced by the `set_space_public_page_default()` BEFORE INSERT trigger, since a column DEFAULT can't reference another column of the same row; the page-BUILDER itself, `PageTabsEditor`, is unconditional for all four kinds, only this default differs]; `cohort_of` [→ collections, when this space is a course cohort], `term`; `findable`/`assistant_readable`/`content_ai_default`/`content_download_default` [default true, mirror the same-named `profiles` columns — a space's own Privacy section, `SpaceProfile.tsx` backstage]) + `space_members` (role enum super_admin|admin|member; `duties` text[] — null = full admin, v1 keys `library`/`courses`/`members`). Creator becomes super_admin via `handle_new_space` trigger; one super_admin per space. `set_member_role()` is the only door for granting/scoping roles (super-admin-only).\n- **A super admin has TWO doors at the foot of the backstage: TAKE OFFLINE and DELETE** (2026-08-17 — a member asked the help room how to delete a group and the honest answer had been \"you can't\"; the founder then added the softer door: \"if they just don't want the Group, Place, etc live but aren't sure they want to delete it yet\"). Plain buttons, super_admin only, inline confirm each — never accordion sections (there is never more to say than the act). **Take offline** → `take_space_offline(p_space)` sets `spaces.status='offline'` (+`status_changed_at/by`); the space is INVISIBLY GONE — `space_alive(id)` (SECURITY DEFINER) gates the read policies of `spaces`, `space_members` (which alone hides it from every member's lists and the posts audience arm), `posts` (author_space_id), `events` (owner_space_id), `resources`, `collections`, and `is_chat_member()` itself (one choke point: chat, messages, reactions, `chat_unread_counts`) — while every row persists. The ONLY way back is Profile → **Off the network** (`my_offline_spaces()` RPC, shown only when non-empty; `/profile#offline`, the bell links there): **Put back online** (`restore_space`) or **Delete**. `is_space_admin`/`is_space_member` read the table directly, so the super-admin check survives the hidden membership. **Delete** → `delete_space(p_space)`, permanent and immediate. Both refuse with a reason the person can act on — the server's message IS the copy: treasury still holds Current (send it on first — the float rule; value is never parked in limbo either way), the space stewards a member (hand them to another steward — a being must always have one), an open trade (finish or cancel). Nested groups are NOT a refusal on delete: they become standalone (the FK already said so; the confirm mentions it only for community/organization). Delete cleans what FKs can't reach: polymorphic edges AT the space (mycelium/recommendations/saved_items), members' per-space `assistant_consent` rows, closed exchanges where the space was a party (their set-null would trip the not-self CHECK; the ledger keeps the money history), booking types whose only audience was the space (narrowed to `mycelium`, never widened), and posts authored AS the space (its own voice goes with it; posts merely addressed to it cascade via `posts.space_id`). Ledger history stays — append-only. Lands on that kind's directory after. ⚠ New read policies on anything hanging off a space should include the `space_alive` gate, or an offline space leaks through that table. A person's own account has neither door yet (Privacy/Terms say email connect@) — a different act with a different promise (prompt, not held), its own build.\n- Membership is **request + approval**: `space_membership_requests` (`initiated_by=self` → admin approves via `approve_join_request()`; `initiated_by=admin` → invitee accepts via `accept_space_invite()`, which requires the initiator be an admin — a bare member suggestion can't self-accept). A third INSERT-policy arm lets any member file a *suggestion* for someone else; admins turn it into a real invite via `endorse_member_suggestion()`.\n- Nesting is **consensual**: `space_nesting_requests` (a group is created standalone immediately; parent admins approve via `approve_group_nesting()` or release later via `eject_group()`; trigger `enforce_parent_consent` blocks non-consensual parent writes).\n- `space_section_shares` (pk space+post+area; pending/approved/declined) — a space's Courses/Library sections show only space-authored posts plus duty-approved member shares; `decide_section_share()` RPC.\n\n### Chat\n- `chats` (kind organization|community|group|place|care_team|direct|event|help) + `chat_members` (synced from `space_members` via trigger; `last_read_at` = per-member read cursor) + `chat_messages` (realtime enabled). RLS goes through the `is_chat_member()` helper to avoid recursion. `ensure_direct_chat()` for 1:1 DMs. `mark_chat_read(chat)` bumps the cursor and clears that chat's notifications. `chat_unread_counts()` RPC powers inbox pills.\n- `profiles.assistant_readable` gates whether **other members'** assistants can read your message *content* in a cross-chat briefing — your own assistant always sees your messages; the fact you wrote (not the content) still counts for someone whose flag is off.\n\n### Care\n- `care_team_members` (patient_id, caregiver_id, status pending|active, initiated_by — either party can initiate via `offerCareFor()`, the other approves; activation creates/joins the care-team chat). `care_invitations` (email invites for non-members; `claim_care_invitations()` on signup). `care_posts` (WOW 0–100 scores + Kindnesses-of-Care recurring board). **The WOW kicks off with a SELF-evaluation** (founder 2026-08-14): all six dimensions (Mental/Physical/Social/Spiritual/Economic/Environmental — `WOW_DIMENSIONS`, they predate this) in the member's own words with an optional self-score each; every answered dimension becomes a wow post AUTHORED BY THE PATIENT (`SelfAudit` in Concierge.tsx, shown on your own board until you've authored something; `/concierge/wow/edit` is the self-composer route — no `:patientId` = your own board). RLS gained the matching self-arm (insert/update/delete `author_id = auth.uid() AND patient_id = auth.uid()` alongside the caregiver arms) and `care_posts_kind_shape` no longer requires a score on wow posts (words-only entries are real). **Scores are a NOW-reading, not a GPA** (founder asked \"running average?\" — answered no): each dimension averages entries from the last 90 days (`WOW_WINDOW_DAYS`, self + care team weighted equally), a quiet dimension carries its latest older entry forward, overall = avg of the six currents; history stays in the feed for a future trend view. The Financial position card stays separate/structured; its own not-shared state now says the trade-off out loud (no rebalancing economy, no care-team help with that piece — honest copy, deliberately not an enforced gate yet). **The self-driving window** (founder 2026-08-14, same conversation: \"allow humans to trust you automating it... kinda like self driving cars\"): a member may hand the window to Claude — `care_settings` (patient-owned row, care-team SELECT via `is_on_care_team`; `wow_window_days` 14–120 / `wow_window_auto` / `wow_window_reason` / `wow_window_set_at`) + the `wow-window` edge function (caller is ALWAYS the patient, no target param; requires `wow_window_auto` already on; throttled server-side to one model call per 7 days, so no daily-cap bookkeeping; reads only dates/dims/scores, never the words; clamps Claude's pick and stores it WITH its one-sentence reason — a tuned window with no reason would be a hidden model again). UI is the `.wowwin` line under the radar chips (own board only): \"Scores read your last 60 days · Let Claude tune it\" ⇄ \"Claude tunes your window as you evolve — currently N days. '<reason>' · Take the wheel back\"; a stale window (>7d) re-tunes quietly on arrival. Caregivers render the client's radar through the same window (they read `care_settings`), keeping every viewer's numbers identical. ⚠ max_tokens matters: 300 silently truncated the reply into the fallback; it's 600 now. `on_call_roster(patient)` (SECURITY DEFINER — gated to the patient or a fellow active caregiver).\n\n### Membership & subscriptions\n- `subscriptions` (tier community|concierge, source gift|stripe, status active|past_due|canceled, `current_period_end` — gifts reuse it as their end date). Admin RPCs `gift_subscription(email, tier, months?)` / `revoke_subscription()` (deletes the row — does NOT touch Stripe billing). `membership_gifts` — pending gifts keyed to an invitee's email, claimed via `claim_gifts_for_email(user, email)` (the shared loop; `claim_membership_gift()` is a thin JWT-email wrapper, and `claim_invite()` calls it with the TOKEN's invitee_email so a gift lands even when someone signs up under a different address). `grant_growth_gift()` — every member gets one 3-month Concierge gift automatically (self, on-conflict-do-nothing so it's truly once); called from the App gate right before it would redirect to `/membership`.\n- Admin membership toolbox (`/admin/supporters`, 2026-08-11): \"Find a member\" searches ALL members via `admin_search_members()` (SECURITY DEFINER — emails aren't in the column grants) and gives per-member actions: gift/upgrade/extend/revoke, and for Stripe members **Override with a gift** / **Revoke & cancel** — both route through the `admin-cancel-stripe` edge function (admin-JWT-gated, cancels Stripe immediately). `stripe-webhook` treats an active `source='gift'` row with null stripe ids as a deliberate admin override and won't clobber it with renewal/deleted events.\n- Membership gate (`App.tsx`, session-cached ref): signed-in + onboarded + non-admin needs an active/past_due subscription or a live gift, else → `/membership`. `GATE_EXEMPT` = auth flows + `/membership` + `/help` + `/donate` + `/privacy` + `/terms` + `/about`. Admins always bypass. Signed-out visitors can still browse public content.\n\n### Invitations\n- `invite_tokens` (token, invitee_email, `opened_at` [stamped by anon-callable `mark_invite_opened()` when the emailed link lands on `/signup`], claimed_by/claimed_at, for_minor) — signup is invite-gated. Claiming is **server-side first** (2026-08-11 truth repair): `handle_new_user()` claims email-matching invites at signup (incl. the mycelium weave); `claim_invite(token)` covers different-address signups (guardianship, weave, gift delivery, inviter bell) and is retried from `App.tsx` until it succeeds (localStorage token only cleared on success). `send-invite` un-mints its token if Resend rejects — an invite row always means an email actually went out.\n- `/invite` (Invite.tsx): ONE \"Invitations across Lichen\" list, per-row status invited → opened → joined; \"At the door\" = `join_requests` still `status='new'` (send resolves the knock only after a successful send); declined knocks step out of view. `join_requests` writes go only through the `join-request` edge function.\n\n### Content, posts & marketplace\n- `posts`: author, optional `space_id`, `audience_space_ids`, `visibility`, `content_type` (`social` / `actionable` drive the live UI split — Compose's two big face cards; `creative`/`educational`/`qa` persist on old posts only, no longer chosen at creation), `service_areas[]` (marketplace/work/courses/food/art/events/places/library/travel), `details` jsonb (area-specific: `modes[]`/`mode` [primary], `price`, `condition`, `availFrom`/`availTo`, `fulfillment`, `deliverRadiusMi`, `paymentPlan`, `tradeTags`, `categories[]`, `location`/`geo`, `meetingUrl`, `online`/`inPerson`, `quiet`, `demo`, `styleTags`, `giftTo`, `modeNotes`, `allocation`, `modules` [course lesson groups]).\n- Marketplace modes are **multi-select**: gift, trade, rent, lend, borrow, sliding-scale, sale, plus ISO (\"in search of,\" demand-side). `details.modes` = everything selected; `details.mode` = primary by precedence `lichen > gift > trade > lend > rent > borrow > iso > paid`. **Lichen\\*** (\"entrusted offering\") is exclusive — selecting it hands allocation to Lichen's Routing Desk (`/admin/supporters` → RoutingDesk.tsx: scores entrusted offerings against open ISOs, steward acts on the top matches; human-in-the-loop v1 of a future autonomous router). `inkind_donations` covers tax-deductible in-kind gifts *to Lichen itself* (distinct from a Lichen\\* marketplace listing).\n- A trigger (`match_marketplace_post()`, AFTER INSERT on `posts`) is the deterministic ISO matcher: a new public offer/ISO bells matching open ISOs/offers on stemmed-lexeme title+body overlap, 90-day window.\n- `hidden_posts` (owner-only, no FK — hides survive post deletion) + `saved_items` (polymorphic, strictly owner-only RLS — no counts or signals visible to anyone, including the author).\n- `style-tags` edge function (Claude vision, a controlled ~40-word vocabulary) tags marketplace photos into `details.styleTags` on publish — fire-and-forget, never blocks the post. `listing-autofill` edge function suggests category/condition/tradeTags from title+body text (Compose's \"✨ Suggest details\" button; pre-checked chips the member can uncheck).\n- Trust vs Recommend (current design): **trust is person-to-person only and private** — no shield anywhere on orgs/groups/communities/places, only on people. **Recommend** is available on any entity or post and is the public amplify signal. Mycelium (\"your web\") = plain membership; vouching = trust, a separate boolean that auto-adds to your web (unvouching withdraws trust but leaves any recommendations). The endorsement overlay everywhere is a query: `(endorsers of item) ∩ (your mycelium)` — always \"what my web endorses,\" never a global score. No counts or leaderboards anywhere, by design. `mycelium.vouched=true` is structurally blocked for `target_type='space'` (a CHECK constraint, not just UI omission) — and, since 2026-08-13, for a space TRUSTER too (`mycelium_space_cannot_vouch`): a space has a web but holds no trust. **A space's own web** rides `mycelium.truster_space_id` (nullable FK → spaces, ON DELETE CASCADE), mirroring `recommendations.recommender_space_id` — the space weaves, `truster_id` still records which human did it. The old PK is gone (nothing referenced it), replaced by two PARTIAL unique indexes — `(truster_space_id, target_type, target_id) where truster_space_id is not null` and `(truster_id, …) where truster_space_id is null` — so a space weaves a target once and any of its admins can undo it, while personal edges keep their old key. ⚠ A partial unique index can't be inferred by `ON CONFLICT`, so `setVouch` does update-then-insert rather than upsert; don't \"simplify\" it back. Its SELECT RLS is your own rows (`truster_id = auth.uid()`) plus, for space rows only, `is_space_member(truster_space_id, …)`; writes to a space row need `is_space_admin`. A space's web starts CLOSED (members read, admins write) — opening it to anyone who can see the space is a one-line policy change if the founder wants it. — the 2-hop \"trusted by someone I trust\" check reads anyone else's edges only via `trust_edges_for_targets()`, a `SECURITY DEFINER` RPC scoped to specific targets already in view (a search result, a listing's seller), never a whole-graph read. `src/lib/trustPath.ts`'s `loadTrustEdgesFor()` is the client wrapper — merge its result into a `TrustWeb`'s `edges` before calling `trustPathTo()`.\n- Home and My-celium both lead their icon row with a lit **Feed** door; the old ALL/SOCIAL/ACTIONABLE tabs were retired — `content_type` stays in the DB (drives Compose's actionable/social split, the marketplace auto-add, and the ISO matcher) but no longer filters the feed.\n- Demo/seed content (a small cast of example members + spaces, see `supabase/demo_content.sql` / `demo_cast.sql`) is marked `details.demo=true` and renders a dismissible EXAMPLE bubble (`.ex-bubble`) on FeedCard/ListingTile/ListingRow; hides via the normal `hidden_posts` mechanism. A one-block wipe SQL sits at the bottom of `demo_cast.sql` for when alpha content needs clearing.\n- Card renderers: `FeedCard.tsx` (stream view), `ListingTile.tsx` (grid/browse view — square photo tiles, typographic covers for text-only listings), `ListingRow.tsx` (job-board rows, used by Work). `AreaFeed.tsx` is the generic area-scoped feed component (`area` prop) powering Marketplace/Courses/Library/Art/Work/Food/Travel.\n\n### Collections, courses & library\n- `collections` (owner, name, description, `is_public`, `space_id` [space-owned], `kind` `'collection'|'course'|'path'` [`'path'` displays as \"Ordered collection\" — DB value unchanged], `details` jsonb — level/format/length/forWhom/price/coverUrl/`modules`). `collection_items` (polymorphic target, `position` = order). **Publish to any room** (founder 2026-08-14, the Drive conversation): CollectionPage's publish button is a ROOM CHOOSER (Feed/Library/Courses/Marketplace) — picking one makes the collection public and routes into `/compose?collection=<id>&area=<room>`, where the room's own flow shapes a door-POST carrying `details.collectionId` (Compose prefills title/body from the collection, shows a receipt banner, and lands you back on the collection). `postOpenPath` sends a collectionId post to `/collections/<id>`; FeedCard shows a \"Collection\" badge (`isCollection` via `postToCard`). \"Make private\" stays the unpublish (door posts then open the collection's not-available state — acceptable, known). **Weaveable consent** (same conversation — weaving is ALWAYS by reference, so attribution is structural and revocation real): whether a post may appear in OTHER people's collections is the author's call — `posts.details.noWeave` (stored only when switched OFF, Compose's fourth content control) preselected from `profiles.weaveable_default` (Profile → Privacy third content-default), ENFORCED by the `enforce_weaveable()` BEFORE INSERT trigger on `collection_items` (catches the picker, lesson picker, Organize, Compose organize-into, and `resolve_collection_suggestion` — the resolver's uid is the steward, not the author; your own posts always weave). `CollectPrompt`'s picker pre-checks and shows \"«Name» keeps this piece out of others' collections\" instead of folder rows. Attribution-credit-as-Current stays parked with the economy design. `collection_enrollments` + `collection_progress` (learner-private RLS). `collection_suggestions` (member-submitted pieces; `resolve_collection_suggestion()`).\n- **A course has an Admin view and a course view** (founder 2026-08-15, \"there's no public course profile\"): the old naked row (Edit / Add lessons / New cohort / Make private / Delete) sat in front of every learner; it's backstage now at `?manage=1`, in the same `CollapsibleSection` accordion Profile and a space use — **Course Builder & Editor**, **Privacy**, **Cost & access**, Lessons, Cohorts, Publishing, Suggested by members, Delete — with ONE save bar for the lot (no per-section buttons) and a single blue \"Manage this course\" pill as the door. Privacy splits the old single `details.protectedTeaching` switch into its three real promises (`details.shareable` / `downloadable` / `aiReadable`, absent = open); the legacy bundled flag still closes all three, so old courses keep the promise they were published under, and the header names WHICH door is shut rather than one blanket word.\n- **A course reads as a SYLLABUS** (founder 2026-08-15: \"you almost check mark your way through the course\"): modules in order with their own progress, each lesson a row you tick, the next one marked \"Up next\". Curator affordances (reorder, module select, remove) ride the same rows in Admin view only. Plain (unstructured) collections keep the FeedCard stack.\n- **Course notes + a self-organizing Drive** (founder 2026-08-15): the ADMIN|COURSE-view toggle sits top-left in BOTH views (Profile's placement; the old \"Manage this course\" pill is gone) and Start/Continue sits top-right with a compact `n/total` — no wide CTA bar. A syllabus row's chevron sits LEFT with the tick so the row's right side carries a per-piece notes bookmark; the top panel is the SUMMARY (every note, each naming its piece and linking to the course's Drive folder, plus a whole-course composer). `course_notes` (profile+collection, optional `post_id` for a per-lesson note) is private by construction — RLS `profile_id = auth.uid()`, no visibility branching, so there's no audience to get wrong. Enrolling fires `ensure_course_folder()` on `collection_enrollments`, creating a private `collections` row named for the course and tagged `details.forCourse` — an ordinary folder you can rename, fill or throw away; the trigger only fires on enroll, so a deleted folder stays deleted. The notes panel names it.\n- **ONLY A DECISION TO POST MAKES A STORY** (founder 2026-08-15, after a first pass made course material a compact activity ROW and Home became a wall of 21 of them — \"notifications should be turned off completely for something as banal as me posting a module... administrative and managerial work around posting courses, etc, shouldn't be in there at all, ever\"): course material never enters the RIVER at all. `loadFeed({river:true})` drops `service_areas ⊇ courses` server-side, alongside the `details.quiet` filter — Home and My-celium are the only river callers, so Courses/collections/search/Drive keep every piece. The ONE exception is a door post (`details.collectionId`), which is exactly the deliberate announcement Compose mints. ⚠ No notification ever fired for posting a module — the only bell on `posts` INSERT is `handle_section_shares` asking a steward to approve a share from someone WITHOUT the duty, which is a real request, not noise. Historical note: the activity-row rendering below still exists and is what the Courses room's feed view uses, but it no longer appears in the feed. Original note (founder 2026-08-15: \"Galyn posted Module 6 to the course library... Module 6's content is not a story\"): a post whose `service_areas` include `courses` maps to `activity`/`activityWho` in `postToCard`, and FeedCard early-returns a one-line `.feed-activity` row (who did what → the piece) instead of the full card. A post carrying `details.collectionId` keeps its card — the door-post IS the announcement. The row spans the feed grid (`.feed-card-shell--activity`) and wraps to two lines rather than truncating: ⚠ the app-shell column stays 430px well past 1024px, so a viewport media query can NOT tell a row how much room it has.\n- A **cohort** is a `spaces` row of kind `group` tagged `cohort_of` → a course/path collection, with a `term` — not a new `space_kind`. Each cohort is a real group (its own chat/calendar/consent flow); a course can have many cohorts over time.\n- **External resources** (founder 2026-08-10: \"much of it will be hosted outside of lichen, until we become a popular platform\"): a Library post can point at content hosted elsewhere instead of being fully re-hosted. Compose's Library area gets a \"Link to an external resource\" field (`Compose.tsx`), resolved through the existing rich-link-preview pipeline (`resolvePreviews`/the `link-preview` edge function — the same one care posts and any body-pasted URL already use) rather than a new unfurl system. Sets `details.isResource = true` (FeedCard shows an \"External resource\" badge, `postToCard` in `feedMapping.ts` exposes it) and `details.previews` (the OG card). `ListingTile`'s browse-grid falls back to the resolved preview's image when there's no uploaded `media` photo, so resource tiles aren't bare typographic covers. Still organizable into collections via the existing \"Organize into\" compose flow — no new curation mechanism needed.\n\n### Presence\n- **Three states: PRESENT, AVAILABLE, and ELSEWHERE** (founder 2026-08-13/14). \"Elsewhere\" is the NAME of the neither-present-nor-available state (founder 2026-08-14) — use it in docs, code, and any future UI that must label the state itself (member rows, directory groupings); Home's greeting renders an all-elsewhere network as \"out living\" (see below), not the word \"elsewhere\". The word \"awake\" is retired — \"it sounds a bit off, like either they're enlightened, or they're sleeping when not on Lichen.\" The four RPCs are `network_present_count`/`_list` and `space_present_count`/`_list` (old `*_awake_*` names dropped, not aliased).\n  - **PRESENT** = `(presence_always_present or presence_lit_until > now()) and last_seen_at > now() - interval '5 minutes'` — here NOW, not here today. Both arms take the freshness guard, so a hand-lit candle no longer outlives the session that lit it. `profiles.presence_visible` and the old \"around\" dot are retired (column stays, unread): nothing shows that someone is merely online. The candle **defaults on** and the existing cohort was backfilled, so present means *online and hasn't snuffed* — honest only because `PresencePrompt` teaches the gesture on first open, once a day, for the **first 3 visits** (`member_prompts.times_seen`), then goes quiet forever.\n  - ⚠ **The window and the heartbeat are a pair.** `AuthProvider.tsx` beats `last_seen_at` every **2 minutes and only while the tab is visible** (plus immediately on `visibilitychange` back to visible). 5 minutes is 2.5× the beat — shorten the window below ~2× the beat, or slow the beat without lengthening the window, and presence STROBES for someone sitting right there. Change them together. Visibility-gating is what makes it true rather than merely fast: a backgrounded tab or a pocketed phone stops beating, so it stops claiming you're open to being interrupted.\n  - ⚠ **The Browser-pane preview reports `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'`**, so the heartbeat never fires there and presence always reads 0 while testing. Not a bug — fake it with `Object.defineProperty(document,'visibilityState',{value:'visible',configurable:true})` + `dispatchEvent(new Event('visibilitychange'))`, which is how the beat→204→count round trip was verified.\n  - **AVAILABLE** = inside your published **social** hours, minus what's booked. Asks nothing of you at the time — set your hours, close the app (\"I just want people to be offline as much as possible, but be able to signal when they're available\"). `availability_windows.kind` now carries three: `available` (work, bookable), **`social`** (what Home counts), `on_call` (the care rota, not subtracted by bookings). All edited in **Calendar settings**, which already had the weekly-hours editor — never add a second one in Profile. Matched in the MEMBER's own timezone (`profiles.timezone`), gated by `calendar_level()` so availability is never public, and **disjoint from present** (present wins; nobody is counted twice). The booked-subtraction happens CLIENT-side in `presenceApi.availableList()` because recurrence lives in exactly one engine (`src/lib/recurrence.ts`) and a SQL expander would fork it — the SQL returns in-hours candidates plus their local date/minute, the client drops anyone busy via `free_busy()` + `occursOn()`. Revisit at thousands of members.\n  - **Nobody is available or bookable by default** (founder 2026-08-14): `availability_windows` starts empty and no-hours means NOT available — unknown is never yes, the platform-wide rule. Find-a-time (\"Everyone free?\") counts only members with real signal (declared work/social hours, or busy time their `calendar_shares` let the viewer see; on-call never counts as meeting availability), shades 7am–9pm only, and a legend names the coverage (\"Going on N of M members' shared hours…\"; zero signal = no shading, just the truth). BookSession with `windows.length === 0` says \"«name» hasn't set up their availability hours yet\" + **Let them know**: a `notify('booking_nudge', …)` bell (client-callable, link → `/calendar/settings`) plus a prefilled DM via `?draft=` on the chat thread (`ChatConversation` prefill, member sends it themselves — the platform has no voice in chat). Demand becomes the setup moment, the candle pattern again.\n  - Home reads \"*N are present and M are available*\"; at zero it reads \"**Your network is out living.**\" (founder 2026-08-13: nobody here is a GOOD sign — \"a utility for healthy, real engagement in the world, not a social network that's addictive\"; \"resting\" implied being here was the natural state, the same trap as \"awake\"); work hours never reach that line (Home is for connection, not commerce). Acting as a space, the count is that space's own members, present only — a space doesn't publish hours, its members do. Neither tier gates messaging: they set expectations. Founder — \"you can always still message me of course, but I'm not going to reply.\"\n\n### Resources (bookable rooms/things)\n- `resources` (one-owner CHECK: `space_id` XOR `owner_profile_id`; kind room|thing; bookable; approval request|instant) + `resource_bookings` (parties-only read RLS, no client writes). RPCs: `request_resource_booking`, `decide_resource_booking`, `cancel_resource_booking`. `events.owner_resource_id` widened the one-owner CHECK to profile|space|resource — a resource has its own calendar. `resource_busy()`/`resource_span_contact()` expose free/busy without leaking who booked what; a booker can be messaged only through the deliberate contact door.\n\n### Calendar, events & bookings\n- Shared recurrence engine (`src/lib/recurrence.ts`, RRULE-lite + `occursOn()`) powers calendar events, reminders, and the `fire-reminders` edge function alike.\n- `calendar_shares` (audience rules, most-specific-wins) + `free_busy()`/`availability_of()` RPCs. `external_calendars` (ICS import via the `sync-external-calendar` edge fn; imported blocks carry `external_busy.source_url` — Google's per-event `htmlLink` [the API `fields` mask was silently dropping it] or an ICS `URL:` property — so the event popup offers \"Open in Google Calendar\", falling back to that DAY in Google when the source gave no per-event link. ⚠ A Google deep link resolves against WHICHEVER ACCOUNT THE BROWSER IS SIGNED INTO — an event in `galyn@galynburke.com` opened from a `connect@lichen.health` session gives \"Could not find the requested event\", which reads as a broken link but is a wrong-account one. Three things address it, all in `Calendar.tsx`: build against `calendar.google.com` DIRECTLY (the legacy `www.google.com/calendar/event` endpoint drops added query params and hardcodes `u/0` on redirect), pass `authuser`, and NAME the owning account under the link — it's the second half of the eid, base64 of `\"<eventId> <calendarId>\"`. \"Or open that day\" is the door that needs no event permissions at all) + `calendar_shares.external_calendar_id` — an imported calendar's visibility is capped at busy-only unless it explicitly opts into `share_titles`.\n- An event = a `posts` row (`content_type='actionable'`, `service_areas ⊇ ['events']`) linked via `posts.linked_event_id` to a real `events` row. RSVP = `event_attendees` (going/tentative/declined), gated through `is_event_attendee()` (SECURITY DEFINER — the reusable pattern for any RLS cycle between two tables that reference each other). Event chat (`chats.kind='event'`) syncs its roster via the `sync_attendee_to_event_chat` trigger. Host edits always go through `updateEventDetails()` — never `updateEvent()`, whose invitee-sync wipes RSVPs.\n- `reminders` (private, owner + shared via `reminder_recipients` type-ahead) + `reminder_done` (keyed per reminder+profile+date — each recipient ticks their own occurrence) + `reminder_fired` (cron dedup claim). `notify_reminder()` bells recipients. Reminders are **never** busy and never appear in free/busy. **TASKS shipped 2026-08-14** on this machinery: (1) timing tiers named in the composer — free to-do = no time, day reminder (`at_min` null) = a FINISH-BY task with a morning nudge, timed reminder = exact time; (2) ASSIGNMENT is live — `listReminders` no longer filters to owner (RLS returns own + shared-to-you, rows carry `owner.full_name`; the client had never loaded shared rows though RLS allowed it for months), assigned tasks render in To-Do/grid with a \"from «name»\" tag, and YOUR OWN tasks say who else is on them (\"with Gabe Miltner, Claude\" — `loadRecipientsFor` batches the whole list, never one query per row; founder 2026-08-14: the row has room, don't make people click through), **one job, shared** by default — whoever ticks it closes it for everyone and the row says \"done by «name»\" (founder 2026-08-14: \"if I mark the task complete, or Gabe does, I assume it disappears for both of us?\"); `reminders.done_mode` = `shared|each` flips to the each-of-us shape (\"everyone submit your hours\") via a composer toggle shown once someone's on the task. Done rows stay per-person (they record WHO), `is_on_reminder()` (SECURITY DEFINER, the 42P17 rule) widens `reminder_done` SELECT to everyone on the task, and reopening a shared job clears whoever's tick closed it — never on an each task, where their tick is their own record, and a recipient can STEP OUT (`leaveReminder` → the \"reminder_recipients leave\" delete-own-row policy; no pending-state machinery — the bell announces, leaving is one tap, the owner's task is untouched); (3) VISIBILITY — `task_shares` (audience everyone|**mycelium**|space|profile, levels hidden|see, one-rule-per-audience coalesce index) + `task_level()` (specificity profile > space > mycelium > everyone, most-RESTRICTIVE wins at equal specificity, **default hidden** — a task list is undone work) + `visible_tasks_of(owner)` (the one read door: open todos + reminder rows for client recurrence expansion). (4) the **SMART COMPOSER** (founder 2026-08-14): the To-Do quick-add reads a whole sentence — \"return amazon package to staples in Conifer and add Gabe Miltner to the task\" — into title + day + time + repeat + real people. DETERMINISTIC like `smartSearch.ts` (`src/lib/taskParse.ts`, same scan/claim/consumed idiom: recognized phrases are consumed and WHAT'S LEFT IS THE TITLE, so the member's own words survive) — no AI call, no cost, nothing leaves the device. The reading is always SHOWN as chips before anything is created, a bare line stays a plain to-do, and a name only becomes an assignee if `resolveAssignees` finds exactly one real match — an unmatched name stays in the title rather than vanishing. A quiet \"Add a time, a repeat, or assign it to someone\" line carries typed words into the full composer via `?title=`. `TaskShareRules.tsx` is the editor (Calendar settings → \"My tasks — who sees them\"; the mycelium tier appears HERE first — calendar_shares still lacks one); To-Do's \"See someone's list…\" type-ahead renders an admitted list read-only, and a private one says so honestly.\n- Bookings (the Calendly-style layer): `booking_types` (audience everyone|mycelium|**public**|**space** [+ `audience_space_id` — one space's members only, \"office hours for the barn\"; visibility routes through `booking_type_visible()` AND the \"booking_types visible\" RLS policy — CHANGE BOTH, the public-link migration forgot the policy and public types were invisible to signed-in browsers for a day]; approval request|instant; the editor's order is Anyone → Anyone on Lichen → My-celium → Members of one of your groups) + `bookings`, all writes through SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (`booking_board`, `create_booking` — server revalidates window containment, overlap, and buffer). No payments yet. **The public booking link** (founder 2026-08-14, \"a calendly replacement... a true, real time snapshot of their availability\"): `lichen.health/book/<handle>` works SIGNED OUT — `/book/:param` disambiguates by shape (uuid → the member slot picker `BookSession`, else → `BookPublic`). Guests book with name+email; `bookings.booker_id` is nullable now with `guest_name`/`guest_email`/`guest_token` (the event_guests unguessable-token pattern; CHECK requires a member OR a guest pair). Anon RPCs: `public_booking_page(handle)`, `public_booking_board` (titleless busy only), `guest_create_booking` (mirrors create_booking's validation), `guest_booking(token)`, `guest_cancel_booking(token)`; `/b/<token>` is the guest's chrome-suppressed landing (status, .ics, cancel). Guest mails ride the `send-booking-mail` edge fn (`verify_jwt=false`; content ALWAYS derived from the row's current DB status — nothing forgeable); providers get normal bells with \"(from outside Lichen)\". ⚠ `respond_booking`/`cancel_booking` were made null-safe — the old `auth.uid() not in (provider, booker)` guard goes NULL (= passes!) with a null booker; `IS DISTINCT FROM` now. Calendar settings shows the copyable link when a public type exists (handle required — no handle, it points to Profile → Public page); a member page's \"Book a time\" CTA falls back to `/book/<handle>` when unset and public types exist (anon-checked via the RPC — RLS hides booking_types from anon). Times render in the PROVIDER's local time with an honest label; guest-side tz conversion is logged polish.\n- `event_guests` — invite people outside Lichen to an event (`send-event-invite` edge fn mints an unguessable token); `guest_event(token)`/`guest_rsvp(token, status)` RPCs are granted to `anon`.\n- Scheduled reminders run on `pg_cron` (`tick_reminders()` every minute) + `pg_net` → the `fire-reminders` edge function, using each recipient's `profiles.timezone`. `push_subscriptions` + the `send-push` edge function deliver web push, triggered by a `pg_net` trigger on `notifications` INSERT — push rides the existing `notify()` call for everything (nudges, DMs, gifts, reminders, all of it), no per-feature wiring needed.\n\n### Current-cy ledger\n- `ledger_entries` (append-only — a trigger refuses UPDATE/DELETE; corrections are offsetting `'adjustment'` entries; polymorphic parties profile|space, designed to extend to non-human entities without a schema change). No INSERT policy — writes only via `send_currentcy()` (self or an admined space, advisory-lock race-safe) and `mint_currentcy()` (admin-only issuance). `ledger_balance()` refuses to reveal anyone else's balance — no leaderboards, by construction, same anti-gamification stance as trust. Architecture: transparent DB ledger + a $1 peg, no blockchain; Stripe Connect payouts are a later phase. Doctrine: never mint more Current-cy than donation dollars actually held (the float rule). **The ledger burns now** (2026-08-13): `to_type`/`to_id` are nullable — from someone, to nowhere — the redemption channel (\"fixed-peg out\"). `burn_currentcy()` mirrors `mint_currentcy()` (admin-only until the member redemption flow exists; same advisory-lock keyspace as every other spend), context `'burn'` joined the CHECK, and `currentcy_float_summary()` reports minted − burned so the float gauge tells the truth once redemptions flow. A burn renders as \"to Lichen\" in statements — `nameOf(null)` already said that.\n\n### Donations\n- `donations` (admin-only read + donor-own-read via RLS; service-role writes). Checkout via the `donate-checkout` edge function (through Lichen's own Stripe; `verify_jwt=false` since donors may be signed out). `translate_donation()` mints 95% as Current-cy (context `'grant'`) and records the other 5% as `central_cents` (operating dollars — deliberately never minted). `keep_donation_for_operations()` for general/operations gifts (100% central, mints nothing). `kind` distinguishes `donation` (Lichen decides recipient — deductible) from `sponsorship` (donor picks the recipient — IRS conduit rule, not deductible; the \"Give\" flow). `inkind_donations` covers non-cash gifts (`accept_inkind_donation()`/`decline_inkind_donation()`, triggers a non-valuing acknowledgment email). `currentcy_float_summary()` is the admin-only float-vs-operating gauge. Auto tax receipts send via Resend from the `stripe-webhook` function, idempotent per donation row.\n- `/giving` — an owner-only dashboard of cash + in-kind giving history and the year's deductible total; nobody sees anyone else's giving (same no-counts doctrine as trust).\n\n### Video hosting\n- Self-run (not a third-party service): the `videos` storage bucket + a `video_jobs` queue (owner-insert, worker-only advance via service role). `worker/` is a Node+ffmpeg poller producing adaptive HLS (rendition dirs are named `vv0`/`vv1`/… — remember this when listing storage) + a poster image; it runs on the founder's Mac today. `worker/ingest.js` is a local-transcode CLI for large source files, bypassing Supabase's free-tier ~50MB upload cap (only works for videos the founder ingests — other members' large files still need Supabase Pro). `VideoPlayer.tsx` (HLS native on Safari, `hls.js` lazy-loaded elsewhere) is wired into FeedCard.\n\n### Search & maps\n- `src/lib/smartSearch.ts` — a deterministic, rule-based sentence interpreter (no AI call): parses trust/recommend degree, price, mode, online/in-person, time windows, place, category, and person names (a trailing name after \"recommended by\"/\"trusted by\" sets that filter; otherwise it scopes by author). The full manual criteria panel covers the same ground and merges additively with a typed sentence. Results show near-misses (posts matching *some* but not all terms) below direct hits, never as a silent substitute.\n- `src/lib/trustPath.ts` — viewer-relative trust computation (direct trust, or one hop via someone you trust). Powers the marketplace \"who you'll do business with\" safety lens (Anyone / trusted-by-someone-I-trust / someone-I-trust, `localStorage 'mkt-trust'`) and the mutual-friend trust line shown on cards/tiles.\n- Maps (Mapbox, lazy-loaded chunk — keep it lazy, the main bundle stays small): event/space/people pins. `location_shares` (per-location-kind audience rules, most-specific-wins) + `location_level()` resolver — visibility ladder `hidden < state < county < area < exact`; `state` deliberately has no pin (findable-not-pinnable); you always see your own location as exact.\n\n### Notifications & assistant\n- `notify()` is the single entry point for every bell (section-scoped: home/profile/calendar/chat/currentcy/membership). `ADMIN_DESK_TYPES` are excluded from the bell UI and unread counts (still written to the DB, still push-delivered) — those surface through each space's own backstage queue instead.\n- The assistant is a real Lichen member account (`claude@lichen.health`) plus a per-entity \"AI Partner\" fabric — two distinct roles, never conflate them in copy. Edge functions: `claude-chat` (legacy 1:1 chat replies, `pg_net` trigger on `chat_messages`), `assistant-feed` (the current door — a member's relationship with Claude as a feed, not a chat thread; `assistant_feed_posts` table, `pg_net` trigger on new member posts there, own daily cap `ASSISTANT_FEED_CAP` default 20/day, `assistant_queries` context `'feed'`), `assistant-search` (narrates search results, context `'search'`), `assistant-brief` (per-section snapshot at `/assistant?section=`, context `'brief'` — and since 2026-08-14 a PERSON briefing at `?section=member&member=<id>`, reached from the brain on another member's profile: \"like getting a briefing on someone you're meeting with\" — the client gathers their profile as the viewer may see it, the viewer's OWN web/trust/recommend signals, shared spaces [RLS makes their memberships visible only where yours overlap], recent non-aiExcluded posts, bookables, and the direct thread — message CONTENT only if their `assistant_readable` allows, else counts+timing with a plain note; cached per person per day; no edge-function change, the client just sends a member frame). `search`/`brief` share `ASSISTANT_DAILY_CAP` (default 30/day); `chat`/`feed` each have their own separate cap — none of the four are pooled together. `AssistantDoor.tsx` is the per-section opt-in/opt-out control (`localStorage 'ai-door-<section>'`) — a section's data is gathered and sent to the assistant **only** when that section's door is on; nothing moves ambiently.\n- `assistant_feed_posts` (profile_id, author `'member'|'claude'`, body, source_post_id, **`thread`** — the room, default `'general'`; free text on purpose so new sections need no migration).\n- Assistant **threads** (founder 2026-08-11, \"since we're weaving a tapestry\" — and note \"rooms\" is already chat's word, so threads it is): the member's feed is threaded by platform section — General, Profile management, Marketplace, Events, Calendar, Concierge (`ASSISTANT_THREADS` in `assistantFeedApi.ts`). Pressing AI inside a section lands in that section's room (`threadForSection`), the reply is written back into the same room, and `general` additionally gets a short read-only glance at the other rooms so it can draw on them. The edge function's system prompt carries a thread rule: off-topic asks get answered briefly plus a pointer to the thread they belong in. The frame is a weave — a thread runs into its section's tapestry and those into the ecosystem, which is what General reads across; a space-scoped thread (Countryman Stables' Marketplace) is the same idea one level in, and the free-text column already allows it. Snapshot is a PANEL at the top of the profile thread (`SnapshotPanel.tsx`) rather than its own screen — `/snapshot` redirects there, and `?back=` carries \"Back to manual mode\". **Role-aware by standing** (founder 2026-08-11): `assistant-feed` reads the member's OWN `space_members` rows and tells the model where they stand — spaces they steward (admin/super_admin, with `duties` named when scoped) get both stewardship and participation help; spaces they're a plain member of get participation help only, with \"ask a steward\" instead of doors they can't open. This is what answers \"whose thread is it\": **the thread is always the member's, and only the HELP changes with role** — so Galyn gets member support inside Melanie's Mentorship Group and both kinds inside WAG. No other member's standing is ever fetched. ⚠ These threads are the MEMBER's own (RLS `profile_id = auth.uid()`), not a space's — per-entity AI Partner threads are still the open vision thread. is private by construction (RLS = `profile_id = auth.uid()`, no visibility branching) — the pattern to reuse for any future closed 1:1-with-Claude relationship, not `posts` (public/space/mycelium only, no private-pairwise mode). `assistantFeedApi.ts` is the client API; `AssistantComposer.tsx` is the shared text+dictation input (`AssistantBrief.tsx`'s inline reply and the feed's own compose box). \"Share to Claude\" (a post's `⋯` menu, wired via `FeedCard`'s `extraMenuItems`) sets `source_post_id` so the reply is informed by what was shared, not just the note.\n- `profiles.assistant_readable` is the *other* consent direction — whether other members' assistants may read what **you** wrote when briefing them (see Chat above).\n\n## Admin\n- `profiles.is_admin = true` gates the admin screens, reached from the Profile page's Admin section (**not** the side menu — the side menu only separates \"you\" doors from platform doors like Invite/Help/Membership):\n  - `/admin/categories` — Review categories (pending category suggestions, approve/reject).\n  - `/admin/supporters` — Memberships & gifts (gift/revoke, through-dates, pending invitation-gifts), DonationsDesk (translate a donation into Current-cy + operating dollars), RoutingDesk (entrusted-offering ↔ ISO matches), MintCurrent (admin-only Current-cy issuance).\n- SideMenu's **Admin view** toggle (blue-ringed, blue desk-count badges) switches the menu to just the spaces you administer, grouped by kind, each linking straight to its `?manage=1` backstage. `listMyAdminDeskCounts()` counts pending section-shares/join-requests/nesting-proposals per space you admin, duty-scoped and actionable-only (outgoing invites never badge — they're awaiting the invitee, not you).\n- Color doctrine: peach = life/engagement, blue = tending the structure — use blue for admin-only affordances (the Manage pill, admin-view badges, the `.is-adminview` primary-button tint).\n\n### Snapshot vs Sync (founder 2026-08-11)\nTwo doors, deliberately different in kind. **Snapshot** (built): a one-time read of what someone already has — talk, type, or paste a URL (their site, an Etsy storefront) — synthesised into a Public Web & Lichen profile they confirm field by field. **Sync & Manage** (next): plugging Lichen into a live backend as hub or spoke, with real inventory. That's stateful two-way sync — credentials, reconciliation, oversell races — and is its own project; the door on `/snapshot` says so rather than pretending. Design calls made: hub-and-spoke, never peer-to-peer sync; **stock should be a ledger, not a mutable number** (same append-only shape as `ledger_entries`); Google Calendar sync is already built and parked on Google's verification, not on engineering. Every builder leads with `BuildModeSplit` — manual on the left (the default, form right below), Build with Claude on the right — plus per-field `FillWithClaude` nudges, and Snapshot always shows \"Back to manual mode\", so someone new to AI can always find the door out.\n\n## Key screens\n- `Onboarding.tsx` — four space-kind sections + provider category pickers (`CategoryPicker.tsx`, searchable, fuzzy-match suggest-new flow). Requires first/last name + phone before it lets you finish.\n- `Profile.tsx` — three toggles, one manage surface (founder 2026-08-11 streamline): **Admin** is the ONLY place content is managed — both kinds; **Lichen View** (→ `/members/<me>`) is the internal member experience (feed, marketplace, events…); **Public View** (→ `/members/<me>?preview=1`) is the website layer of public tabs on top. The same 3-way toggle renders on the member page itself (`MemberProfile.tsx`, isSelf) — Lichen View / Public View switch `?preview` in place, Admin comes back to `/profile`. The old `?view=web` segmented view is gone; its editor (publish toggle, `lichen.health/<handle>` address, tagline, story [+ \"Draft it with Claude\"], get-in-touch actions, cover style, tabs, contact & hours) is now the **Public page** accordion section leading Admin (matching a space backstage's Public Profile Builder); `?view=web` links redirect there. Admin's other sections (About you, Privacy, Notifications, Goods & services you offer, Current-cy, Concierge [care team + people you care for + young people you hold + beings you steward, one accordion item], your 4 space-kind lists, Admin) each render via the shared `CollapsibleSection` component (`src/components/CollapsibleSection.tsx` — lifted from `SmartSearchCore`'s manual-search criteria panel so both share one implementation) — click a header to expand it inline and edit, click again to collapse; deep links like `/profile#privacy`/`#care-for` auto-open their target section. **Acting as a space redirects `/profile` straight to that space's own backstage** (`/spaces/:id?manage=1`, skipped when a hash is present) — Profile is always the settings page for whoever the TopBar says you are (founder 2026-08-10).\n- ⚠ `/chat/:id` (`ChatThread`) is the PHONE's screen: `.thread` is `position: fixed` + viewport-centred at `--app-max`, so beside the sidebar it floats a phone column aligned with nothing. At ≥1024px the route REDIRECTS to `/chat?open=<id>` (the split view), carrying `?from=` — which `closeThread()` honors like the mobile back button. It watches the media query rather than sampling it once (a cold load can run the effect before layout has a width). A cohort group's icon row carries a **Course** door back to its `cohort_of` collection — the toggle the course's own Cohort door needed.\n- `Chat.tsx` / `ChatConversation.tsx` — real Supabase chats + realtime (`src/lib/chatApi.ts`): 1:1 DMs (`ensure_direct_chat`), private media (chat-media bucket, signed URLs), reactions & replies, day dividers, an emoji picker, inbox search that also reaches into message history (`chatApi.searchMessages`). Care-team chat lives in Concierge, event rooms live on event pages, help rooms show only in the support account's inbox.\n- `Help.tsx` (`/help`) — every member gets a private support room with the Lichen help account (`connect@lichen.health`, is_admin) via `ensure_help_chat()`.\n- `Concierge.tsx` — WOW/KOC `care_posts` board (`src/lib/conciergeApi.ts`); Urgent tab (`on_call_roster()`); Care Team tab (directory + management, shared `careTeamApi.ts` also used by Profile); `MeansCard` (financial position, read-only for caregivers).\n- `Events.tsx` / `EventPage.tsx` — category tabs, Free/Trade/Paid circles, About/Updates/Chat/RSVP/Book tabs; RSVP = Going/Maybe/Can't; host gets Edit/Cancel; Compose `?post=<id>` is the edit path.\n- `Calendar.tsx` — Day/3-Days/Week/Month + Schedule (agenda list, phone default) views, drag-to-create (mouse only, no touch yet), additive calendar sources picked SEARCH-FIRST (founder 2026-08-14: too many calendars for a bubble row — only Mine + what's ON render as chips [tap to drop], an inline \"Add a calendar…\" input lists/filters your group memberships on focus (picking one CLOSES the list — completion reads clearly; clicking the box reopens it), and a typed query offers a handoff into the full calendar search for everyone else's; the toolbar is doors-left (Search · + · Brain, Home's order) / calendar-controls-right, all 34px, with the Bookings door showing only once you have booking types; imported Google/ICS calendars are STANDING chips instead (ids `ext:<id>`, never in the picker — founder 2026-08-14: Lichen won't be most people's default calendar for a while, so their Google stays in view, white when off, lit when on, on by default as yourself and off-but-visible acting-as-a-space) — the chip row must tell the truth about every source on the grid; ⚠ the arrival Google-sync reloads through `loadRef`, never a captured `load` — the stale closure repainted Mine's sources over a space's chips once), overlap lanes, find-a-time (unions members across every selected space chip), external ICS import + Google Calendar OAuth (built, currently parked — see Open threads), a To-Do toggle, and reminders (composer Event|Reminder pills, editable, shared nudges via `reminder_recipients`).\n- `CollectionPage.tsx` — course-aware: offering chips (`OfferingChips.tsx`), numbered/modular lessons, a learner enroll+progress loop, an owner metadata editor + lesson reorder + \"Add lessons\" picker, a list of cohorts (each opening its own group chat/calendar), and a curated-section suggestion queue for space-owned collections.\n- `SpacesDirectory.tsx` — serves `/communities /groups /organizations /places`. **Your X / All X** (founder 2026-08-15): the section had no all-of-them view, so its brain had no subject — two toggles under the icon row give each scope a home and the assistant follows via `?mine=1|0` (own cache key, own frame: ALL = what's new + the few that genuinely fit you, told not to pad; YOURS = activity where you're a member, then one concrete stewardship act where you admin). Toolbar is the platform grammar — search · + · brain circles, hairline, then My-celium / Recommended (1st) / Recommended (2nd) text lenses (viewer-relative degree via `trust_edges_for_targets`, scoped to the recommenders in view). The lens row is a `ScrollHintRow` in **fade** mode — it wrapped and orphaned a chip at 380px otherwise. Empty says WHICH empty (no match / no lens hit / not in any yet, with a door to All). The `+` shows only for groups, the one kind created from this page.\n- `SpaceProfile.tsx` — public face (identity, feed, join/trust/mycelium, Rooms & things, a single \"Manage this {kind}\" pill with a desk-count badge for admins) vs. backstage (`?manage=1`, same `CollapsibleSection` accordion Profile.tsx uses — every space kind gets the same section list, founder's 2026-08-10 profile-features spreadsheet: **Public Profile Builder** [name/description/location/contact + the same handle/tagline/CTA-action/cover-style fields Profile's Web-page view has — the old separate \"Edit profile\" toggle button is gone, the section header IS the toggle now], **Privacy** [findable/assistant-readable/content-AI-default/content-download-default, mirroring Profile's own], **Current-cy** [`CurrentcyCard` generalized to accept `partyType`/`partyId` — the ledger already treats spaces as first-class parties (`ledger_balance`/`send_currentcy`/`mint_currentcy` all take a type+id), this was a UI gap, not a backend one], notifications, shared-for-the-shelves queue, waiting-at-the-door, member roles/duties, invite/suggest, group release/nesting proposals). `?tab=members` / `?tab=events` / `?tab=groups` open dedicated sub-pages instead of scrolling the feed — kept as plain sections, not folded into the accordion, since they're reachable both ways. **Concierge (a space's own care team) is deliberately not built yet** — `care_team_members`'s RLS + 3 triggers + its own care-chat creation all hard-assume `patient_id` is a profile; doing this properly means extending those, not just adding a column, so it's its own follow-up.\n- `MemberProfile.tsx` / `MemberAbout.tsx` — public view (`ContributionsFeed`, a clamped bio + \"About & offerings\" door), Trust + Recommend + Message + Book doors, presence signals.\n- `PublicPage.tsx` (the page template) — one shared structure for every Lichen public site (hero → story → offerings → practical info → presence → join), rendered when the viewer is signed out or `?preview=1`. `SpaceByHandle.tsx` resolves `/:handle` to a space's page. Every public page leads with a **Home** tab (founder 2026-08-11: \"you always have to have a homepage to land on\") — for MEMBERS too since 2026-08-14: guests always land on Home; a signed-in member ALWAYS lands on Feed (founder 2026-08-14, choosing one rule over a brief feed-only-when-nonempty experiment: \"I prefer consistency\") — an empty feed says \"No Feed content from X yet!\" with a **Visit the homepage to engage** escape that switches to the Home tab IN PLACE (`ContributionsFeed`'s `emptyEscape` → `ScopeEmpty`'s `onGo`, wired through `FeedRenderCtx.openHome`). **Icons above, toggles below, everywhere** (founder 2026-08-14): for signed-in members the word-tab nav moves OUT of the hero into `FeedRenderCtx.navSlot`, which `ContributionsFeed` renders right under its icon row; guests/preview keep the hero nav (the public website's masthead is its own design). Events made the same swap (category tabs now below its doors/lenses row). Switching Lichen View ⇄ Public View re-lands automatically (a `relandKey` effect on `asGuest` — the old tab could be missing on the other side, which used to blank the page until a hand refresh); a tab the viewer CHOSE sticks (`chooseTab`/`touched`), only automatic landings get replaced. Entity-page area doors (Marketplace/Courses/…) are presence-gated again (founder 2026-08-14, reversing 08-13's always-on: doors into empty rooms read as clutter; ScopeEmpty/ScopeMore still catch anyone arriving by other routes). A pinned space earns a **Place door** in its icon row (founder 2026-08-15 — the Courses rule: a door appears because something is behind it), replacing the old \"See it on Maps\" CTA; the relationship signals (Member ✓ / My-celium ✓ / Recommended ✓) ride the END of that same row via `ContributionsFeed`'s `signals` prop instead of floating above the masthead, and the word tabs left-align under it. Home is the ROOT and the other tabs are BRANCHES: it **teases and routes** — a section that has a tab of its own shows a taste on Home (2 story paragraphs, 5 offerings, 1 facilities paragraph) with a `.ppage__more` link through; a section with nowhere to route shows in FULL, so nothing is ever truncated into a dead end (`teasing(id)` in `PublicPage.tsx`). About/Services/etc are optional doors that hold the whole thing. Skipped when a page drives itself with custom `page.doors`. Its own nav bar owns the `feed` vs `beforeContent`/`children` gating — only `feed` respects the active tab (`showingFeed = showFeed && tab === 'feed'`); `beforeContent`/`children` render unconditionally on every tab, so only genuinely tab-independent content belongs there. The Feed door lives IN the stream's icon row, not the nav (founder 2026-08-11, replacing the earlier nav-icon spot): pass `feed` as a render-function `(ctx: FeedRenderCtx) => node` — PublicPage calls it on EVERY tab with `{showing, open}`, and `ContributionsFeed`'s `feedDoor`/`listHidden` props render a lit `.cfeed__area--feed.is-here` circle in Home's slot (after AI, at the hairline) while hiding the list on non-feed tabs — the persistent row is the way back from About/Services. A plain-node `feed` keeps the legacy `.ppage__nav-icon` behavior; the nav itself stays all-text template tabs.\n- `AssistantBrief.tsx` (`/assistant?section=`) — per-section snapshot + narration, with a door into your Claude feed (`AssistantFeed.tsx`, `/assistant/feed`) — your whole relationship with Claude, replacing the old 1:1 chat thread.\n- `Avatar.tsx` carries an optional **mind mark** (founder 2026-08-17, built but INTENTIONALLY UNWIRED — don't rebuild it): the badge slot holds a steward's FACE when they have a photo, the `pulse` glyph when they don't, and for an assistant always the `chip` — silicon never gets a face, which is what keeps the two distinguishable. Suppressed below 28px. Where to show it is a placement call: good on a place's own page or a chat header, noise on every row of a directory.\n- The install nudge (`InstallPrompt.tsx`) renders **in Home's flow, below the greeting** — not fixed over every route, where it sat on top of whatever you were reading (founder 2026-08-17). It has a 4s delay before appearing, so a fast client-side sweep will look like it's missing.\n- `Saved.tsx` (`/drive`, `/saved` aliases to it) — **DRIVE** (founder 2026-08-14: \"saving something is different than having it in a drive... Drive feels more powerful\"): your private repository — what you SAVED and what you CREATED, one chronological feed (saves sort by when you saved them — `loadSavedPostsTimed`), All/Saved/Created word toggles below the icon row, a lit Feed door, collection folders, search, a Post door. The save GESTURE stays \"save\" (you save TO Drive); only the place renamed. `/organize` is the folder studio.\n- `MyceliumDirectory.tsx` (`/mycelium/directory`) — your whole web grouped by kind, trust shield for people / recommend thumb for spaces, presence controls, weave-from-search.\n- `SmartSearch.tsx` (`/search`) — sentence interpreter + full criteria panel, scoped per-section via `?space=`/`?member=`/`?area=`.\n- **THE WAY BACK IS A PLATFORM RULE** (founder 2026-08-15): entering any section through an entity's filter (`?space=`/`?member=`) shows a persistent \"← Back to «name»\" chip until you leave that scope — `ScopeBack.tsx`, mounted in Marketplace/Events/AreaFeed/MapView, reading the scope straight off the URL so it can't go stale (AreaFeed's bespoke `mkt__memberback` was the precedent and now uses the shared one). Distinct from ScopeEmpty/ScopeMore, which point OUT to the whole section; this points BACK to whoever's view you're in. The TopBar's arrow is a REAL back button too now (React Router's `history.state.idx > 0` → `navigate(-1)`, else Home) — it used to always dump you on Home.\n- `MapView.tsx` (`/maps`) — arriving with `?space=`/`?member=`/`?event=` FLIES to that pin and opens its popup (founder 2026-08-15: a Place door that dropped you on a map of everything nearby didn't answer \"which one is theirs\"). Pins that SAY WHAT THEY ARE (each teardrop carries its kind's mark via `iconSvgMarkup()`, a raw-SVG export of the same `ICONS` table the app uses, so map and app can't drift; the glyph counter-rotates inside the 45°-rotated drop). Toolbar is the platform anatomy: Search · + · AI, a hairline, then layer LENSES in Marketplace's grammar (icon + word + check when on, not filled pills). A member's goods-&-services pin wears the Members mark; spaces wear their kind's.\n\n## Marketing site & partner decks\nSeparate repo: `lichenhealth/lichen-health` (Astro), builds into this repo's `public/`.\n- Ship flow for any marketing-page change: edit `lichen-health` → `npm run build` → commit+push that repo → rsync the changed `dist/` dirs into this repo's `public/` (+ `dist/_astro/`) → commit+push here (Vercel only deploys this repo).\n- Clean URLs: `/care /business /platform` (`ProjectPage.astro` template, three thin pages) replaced the old WordPress-holdover `/project/*` paths, which now 308-redirect.\n- Partner/fundraising decks share one template: `WeavePitch.astro` + `EcosystemStack`, selected via a `variant` prop — `variant=\"about\"` is the full merged story served static at `/about` (shadows the in-app About route for everyone); the default variant is a short per-prospect deck at `/<name>weave`.\n- `/privacy-and-ai` is the public data/privacy/AI-101 page, adapted from the in-app \"Settings 101\" course — keep the two in step when either changes.\n- Optional passphrase protection for a weave page: `scripts/protect-pages.mjs` (staticrypt), opt-in per page via a gitignored `weave-passwords.json`.\n- SEO: `api/page.ts` (a Vercel function) injects real OG/title/description meta for `/spaces/:id` and `/members/:id` shares (fetches the deployed shell, patches meta, returns the same SPA shell so React still boots). Handle-routed pages (`/:handle`) don't have this yet. This is deliberately the smallest fix for link previews/indexing, not an SSR migration — the app is otherwise a client-side SPA.\n\n## Edge functions\n⚠ **Assistants read the docs.** `supabase/functions/_shared/doctrine.ts` is GENERATED from this file (plus `docs/ASSISTANT_ACTIONS.md`) by `scripts/build-doctrine.mjs`, and bundled into any assistant function that talks to members — so their answers are current without a second hand-written description to rot. Regenerate before deploying one:\n```\nnode scripts/build-doctrine.mjs && supabase functions deploy <name>\n```\n⚠ The corollary: **a feature not written here is a feature the assistants don't know about.** Pronouns shipped and CLAUDE.md wasn't updated; the help room correctly said it wasn't sure and deferred, which is the honest failure but still a failure. Updating this file IS shipping.\n\nDeploy with `supabase functions deploy <name>` (works without Docker). Secrets are read from Supabase Edge Function secrets — never hardcoded in the repo. Several call Stripe/Anthropic via raw `fetch` rather than an SDK (SDK HTTP clients can fail in the Deno edge runtime); Stripe secrets get `.replace(/[^\\x21-\\x7E]/g,'')` to survive paste artifacts.\n- `profile-snapshot` — SNAPSHOT (founder 2026-08-11): reads what a member types/dictates plus any public URL they paste (one fetch, HTML stripped to text — no credentials, nothing ongoing) and proposes a whole presence: tagline, story, categories mapped onto the REAL vocabulary sent with the request, contact fields, listings, and plain questions for what it couldn't find. Returns a PROPOSAL only — `Snapshot.tsx` shows every part for confirmation and `applySnapshot()` writes just what's ticked (page/contact merge, `profile_categories` + the capability rows they imply, marketplace posts). ⚠ Parse EVERY text block of the Anthropic reply, not `content[0].text` — a non-text leading block silently yielded an empty proposal.\n- `send-care-invite`, `send-invite` — member/care-team email invites (Resend).\n- `send-event-invite` — invite someone outside Lichen to an event.\n- `send-gift-notice` — gift-carrying invite emails.\n- `stripe-checkout`, `stripe-webhook`, `stripe-portal` — membership billing.\n- `donate-checkout` — donation checkout (`verify_jwt=false`, donors may be signed out).\n- `claude-chat` — 1:1 chat replies, AND the help room. A `help` chat answers without the magic word (nobody should learn one to get support), never answers the steward's own messages, and gets three things the other kinds don't: the `HELP_FRAME` (routing by KIND of question — answer what exists, thank-and-defer what doesn't, decline what's unsure or touches money/care/data), a live ROSTER (each member's presence, whether they've read the latest message, their pronouns, and WHICH of them is the human — in its own UNCACHED system block, since it changes every message), and **read-only lookups**: `my_setup` and `my_spaces`. ⚠ Those tools take NO arguments and are executed against `trigger.sender_id` — there is no target a model could be talked into passing, the same rule the profile-edit tools follow. Bounded to 2 rounds, then `tool_choice: none` forces an answer.\n- `assistant-feed` — the current door: replies in a member's Claude feed.\n- `assistant-search`, `assistant-brief` — search narration and per-section briefings (a PERSON briefing at `?member=`, a COURSE briefing at `?section=courses&collection=<id>` — course, outline in order, and where the viewer stands; ⚠ `collection_items.target_id` is polymorphic with NO FK, so ids first then a separate `posts` read, never an embed).\n- `style-tags` — vision-tags marketplace photos into a controlled vocabulary.\n- `listing-autofill` — AI-suggested listing details from title+body text.\n- `inkind-receipt` — non-cash donation acknowledgment email.\n- `sync-external-calendar` — ICS calendar import.\n- `google-oauth-start`, `google-oauth-callback` — Google Calendar connect (built, parked — see Open threads).\n- `wow-window` — Claude tunes a member's WOW score window (opt-in, throttled weekly, reason stored; see Care).\n- `fire-reminders` — scheduled reminder firing, called every minute by `pg_cron`.\n- `send-push` — web push delivery, triggered by a `pg_net` trigger on `notifications` INSERT.\n\n## Secrets — never hardcode\n`RESEND_API_KEY`, any Stripe keys, the Supabase service-role key, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, Mapbox secret tokens (the public `pk.*` token is fine client-side, like the Supabase anon key) live in Supabase secrets / env, never in the repo.\n\n## Vision (architected, not yet built)\n- **Multi-species entities**: members beyond humans (a therapy horse, a plant). PARTIALLY SHIPPED: `profiles.kind` (person/plant/animal/place/element/collective) + `steward_profile_id`/`steward_space_id` (XOR CHECK; person = no steward) are live, and `MemberProfile` renders beings with a \"Reach «steward»\" door. The family's NAME is **\"Stewarded members\"** (founder 2026-08-14 — literal over beautiful; never \"audiences\", they're members who hold value and accrue contributions). **Jurisdiction** (same day): plants and elements are DISTRIBUTED — in many places at once — so creating one REQUIRES naming the specific scope tended (\"the Skagit watershed\"): `profiles.jurisdiction` (public column, granted like identity_tags; CHECK `profiles_distributed_jurisdiction` + the `create_entity_profile` RPC both enforce it — the RPC gained `p_jurisdiction`, old 4-arg signature DROPPED, one PostgREST candidate). Animals/places/collectives may carry one, plants/elements must (\"each animal is already somewhere\"). Overall/field-level stewards (a species' steward, an element's) are a possible later chapter — `aspect='collective'` (Tango vs Huachuma, settled 2026-07-18) already holds that door open, and steward COMMUNITIES (water stewards, equine stewards) need nothing new: they're ordinary `spaces`. A being's page shows \"Tended within «jurisdiction»\" and wears the recommend thumb, never the trust shield (fixed 2026-08-14 — its page had a Trust button). Demo: Heroes Journey Center re-kinded `collective` 2026-08-14 (it had snuck into the member list as a person with a trust shield). Still open: contributions/value accruing to the entity itself. The Current-cy ledger's polymorphic-party design absorbs this without a schema change.\n- **Per-entity AI Partner fabric**: today there's one Claude member account; the vision is entity-scoped assistants (an org's, a group's, eventually a non-human entity's own AI Partner, via its steward).\n\n## Open threads / next up\n- Acting-as coverage sweep (2026-08-10 audit): the whole experience should follow whoever the TopBar says you're acting as (founder). DONE: `/profile` → space backstage redirect; My-celium → the space's OWN web (built 2026-08-13, see the trust/recommend doctrine above — the earlier bounce-to-profile mitigation is gone); Calendar defaults to the acting space's calendar chip; identity switch stays on the current page (no forced navigation); Home's presence greeting follows the acting space (`space_awake_count`, which counts you) and its door opens My-celium — which, acting as a space, is now that space's own web (founder 2026-08-13: \"have the network tagline go... to Countryman Stable's mycelium\"). STILL OPEN: a space-scoped Chat inbox (a space's own room exists, but `/chat` always shows the person's full inbox — `chat_members` has no space column); Saved is deliberately personal-only (same bucket as care team/financial position). Home's feed staying personal while acting-as is a decided non-bug (see the comment in `Home.tsx` ~line 48).\n- Space Concierge (a space's own care team — the equine therapist for the barn's horses, the soil-rehab specialist for land; founder 2026-08-10 spreadsheet says all 5 entity kinds get Concierge): needs `care_team_members.patient_space_id` alongside `patient_id` (XOR CHECK, the `resources`-style one-owner pattern) plus updates to its 4 RLS policies, 3 triggers, and the patient-keyed care-chat flow. Space financial position also deferred — the household-shaped `financial_positions` doesn't translate; probably a funding-gap disclosure instead.\n- **Present without being in the app** (founder 2026-08-13, parked deliberately — \"there are more important things to do right now\"): presence today requires a heartbeat, so you're only present while Lichen is in front of you. But there's something real in being able to keep your candle lit while you're *not* in the app — \"I'm not looking right now, but I'm reachable if something arises\" is a genuine kind of availability, and it shouldn't cost you having to sit in the app to signal it. Founder's hunch is that it's tied to **notifications being on**: if you'd get a push, you're reachable, and the candle could honestly stay lit on that basis rather than on a heartbeat. The machinery is already there (`push_subscriptions` + the `send-push` edge function), so this is a doctrine question, not a plumbing one: it would split presence into *here now* (heartbeat) and *reachable* (subscribed + candle), and someone has to decide whether those are one signal or two, and what each promises the person on the other side. Not designed yet — do not build without that conversation.\n- Availability setup moments (founder 2026-08-14, ships with the onboarding-consent work): the onboarding flow OFFERS work + social hours (skippable; skipping = none — the default-nothing doctrine above). On Call is NOT an onboarding question — when a care-team membership becomes ACTIVE, that flow points to Calendar settings for On Call details. Also planned: a consent-bubble prompt to finish availability at relevant moments (e.g. a member showing services on their profile with no work hours). The booking-nudge gate is already live and carries the load meanwhile.\n- Trust vs recommend for stewarded members (founder 2026-08-14): \"I dunno if we should think more about the trust versus recommend buttons for elements, plants and animals\" — beings currently wear the thumb only; revisit deliberately.\n- Guest booking page timezone conversion (2026-08-14): the public link shows the provider's local time with an honest label; converting slots to the visitor's timezone is real work (minutes are tz-naive by doctrine) — polish when outside bookers are actually arriving.\n- **THE ONBOARDING-CONSENT FLOW now carries three things, and has a build ORDER** (founder 2026-08-17: \"the onboarding flow process should bring people through privacy, etc, which is another way to help get people fluent with the platform and how to use it as they desire\"). Onboarding orients on the big consents; in-context bubbles decide the rest; both share `member_prompts` so nothing is asked twice. Queued behind it, in the order they were agreed: (1) the trust/recommend walkthrough, (2) work + social availability hours, (3) **AI consent** — which is the newest and the one with a dependency. ⚠ SEQUENCE: the `assistant_consent` table must land BEFORE onboarding presents AI choices, or onboarding will write `localStorage` keys that step 3 of the consent build then has to migrate again. Build the table, then teach onboarding to write to it. The same applies to the in-context toggle on `/assistant` (\"Let the assistant see this section\"), which is the control most members will actually meet — most people never open Profile → Privacy, but they see the brain on every page — so it should become the entry point to the per-scope model rather than staying a single per-device switch.\n- Onboarding trust walkthrough (founder, 2026-08-09): orient new members on what trust/recommend degrees mean (the \"Trusted (1st)/(2nd),\" \"Recommended (1st)/(2nd)\" language on the marketplace filter row) as part of onboarding, rather than explaining it in place — deliberately deferred so it ships together with the rest of the planned onboarding-consent work (onboarding orients on the big consents, in-context bubbles decide the rest).\n- `page.showPosts` (the flag meant to let an owner open their Feed tab to signed-out web visitors) has no write path anywhere — `Profile.tsx`/`SpaceProfile.tsx`'s edit forms never set it, so `PublicPage.tsx`'s Feed tab is invisible to every anonymous visitor on every profile/space today, any kind. Needs a real settings toggle, not a consistency fix — found in the 2026-08-09 architecture audit, not yet built.\n- Marketing-site Stripe Payment Link subscribers aren't in our `subscriptions` table (predates the webhook) — check Stripe periodically and gift them manually, or they'll hit the paywall.\n- Broader RLS/privacy review of remaining tables before public launch — a first pass (2026-08-09) covered spaces/events/chat/mycelium-adjacent policies (see `git log` around that date for what got fixed); still open for the rest of the schema.\n- Event invites to Groups/Places — composer copy promises it, search is still member-only. Also no storage for previews/thumbnails on calendar-only (non-post) event invites.\n- Google Calendar OAuth is built and deployed but parked (`SHOW_GOOGLE_CONNECT=false` in `CalendarSettings`) pending Google's app-verification review — the unverified-consent screen broke for real users. Flip the flag once verification clears; the secret-URL ICS import stays as the universal fallback meanwhile.\n- Calendar drag-to-create is mouse-only; no touch support yet.\n- Urgent-care \"Text\"/\"Call\" today open the patient's own dialer/SMS composer (`tel:`/`sms:` links). An actual server-side send to the caregiver's phone would need a provider like Twilio (account, per-message cost, US A2P registration).\n- Live location (\"where are you right now\") is deliberately the last piece of the Maps privacy ladder — v1 idea is an opt-in, default-off \"last seen near X while using Lichen,\" not real-time tracking (PWAs can't background-track on iOS anyway).\n- \"Near me\" feed lenses (PostGIS-backed proximity search) — not built.\n- A marketplace listing linked to a bookable `resources` row (so its dates are real availability, not just text) + availability search against `resource_busy()` — schema supports it, no UI yet.\n- Course-level AI exclusion: let a teacher mark a course \"never read by the assistant,\" shown to students as a standing promise. The per-section consent machinery already exists; this would extend it into a lineage-teacher guarantee — worth offering whenever a sacred-tradition teacher hesitates about AI involvement.\n- Video: in-app camera + screen recording into the existing ingest pipeline; a self-hosted LiveKit video-call layer wired to Bookings for 1:1 care calls.\n- Donate-back on gifted course content (a scholarship flow) — founder is checking the tax shape.\n- A course \"Provider Studio\" (manage all your offerings in one place), per-standalone-post legibility chips, and cohort scheduling.\n- Compose doesn't default its audience from the current profile/space context yet — always a manual pick.\n- Alpha-data cleanup: delete test posts (SQL is ready; founder to pick a date). The duplicate \"Lichen\" org and duplicate \"The Audacity Lab\" rows are already gone (verified/cleaned 2026-08-11).\n- Recurring-donation renewals (Stripe's `invoice.paid`) aren't recorded yet — only the initial checkout donation is.\n- Inbox realtime refresh (new messages appearing without a manual reload) and the broader \"how much can signed-out visitors browse\" scope decision are both still open.\n- Claude's relationship shipped as a feed (`AssistantFeed.tsx`, 2026-08-09) with \"Share to Claude\" — but only for the member's own relationship. Still open: the full per-entity AI Partner fabric (every group/org/community/place gets its own Claude feed, filtered to that space's own activity the way Marketplace-on-a-Community only shows that Community's Marketplace posts — founder confirmed this is the right shape, 2026-08-09) — needs `assistant_identities` actually wired into the frontend (currently deny-all/unused) and per-space AI consent (today's `aiDoorOn(section)` is per broad section, e.g. all organizations at once, not per specific group). See [[assistant-architecture]] in memory.\n\n- **Per-identity AI consent** (founder 2026-08-17; BUILT same day, in the brief's order — enforcement before UI). \"One group may want to be in the Ai fabric of lichen while another doesn't... Or I may want Ai to be involved for me in community, but not concierge... You can say 'all on' or you can de-select certain aspects of your identity.\"\n  - **The default is ON — opt-OUT, not opt-in** (founder): \"The entire point of lichen is collaboration between Ai and Oi.\" Deliberately the one place the platform's usual \"unknown is never yes\" does NOT apply — participation is the premise, not a permission. \"All on\" = **no rows**; every de-selection is exactly one row.\n  - `assistant_consent` (migration `20260817120000`): pk `(profile_id, scope_type, scope_id)`, scope_type `section|space|aspect` (`aspect` reserved, nothing writes it yet), `scope_id` text so a section name and a space uuid share one column, owner-only RLS. Resolvers (all SECURITY DEFINER): `assistant_consent_for(profile, scope_type, scope_id)` → effective boolean defaulting TRUE; `assistant_consent_all(profile, section, space?)` → the stricter of several scopes; `assistant_consent_care(patient, caregiver)` → `(effective, patient_enabled, caregiver_enabled)`, gated to the two parties, both concierge-level.\n  - **Server-side enforcement** lives in `supabase/functions/_shared/consent.ts` (`assistantConsentOff()` — reads the member's few `enabled=false` rows, answers in code; fails OPEN because default-on is the doctrine and a read hiccup must not read as \"no\"). All four assistant functions check it where the data is gathered: `assistant-brief` (caller's section → `{available:false}`), `assistant-search` (payload carries `section` now; checks it + `'search'`), `assistant-feed` (the thread; the member wrote deliberately, so Claude answers ONCE with the honest off-state note, deduped, never silence), `claude-chat` (sender's `'chat'`/`'help'`; silent skip — the same shape as not being addressed).\n  - **Client**: `src/lib/assistantConsentApi.ts`. `aiDoorOn`/`setAiDoor` (still exported from `AssistantDoor.tsx`) stay synchronous but are backed by the DB: a module cache synced once per sign-in (`syncAssistantConsent()` in `AuthProvider`), with the old `ai-door-<section>` localStorage keys DEMOTED to a per-device mirror of DB state. ⚠ The one-time migration (`ai-door-migrated` flag) pushes a device's pre-existing 'off' keys up with insert-do-nothing, so a stale device can never clobber a choice made elsewhere — and a failed push retries next boot rather than marking done falsely. Turning a scope back ON deletes the row (all-on = no rows); don't \"simplify\" to storing true rows.\n  - **UI**: Profile → Privacy carries the de-selection list (`AssistantConsentList.tsx`, `CONSENT_SECTIONS` = 19 rooms whose ids match the door/thread/server keys — one row governs all three). Concierge's brain (`.conc__brain`) is the REAL concierge-level switch now — it was component state that reset on every mount and controlled nothing.\n  - **Care consent is mutual, and mutually VISIBLE** (founder 2026-08-17: the more restrictive governs AND both sides are told; silence in either direction is the failure). Built: client view shows the caregiver a `.conc__ai-note` banner when their client has concierge AI off (\"no assistant, yours included, reads or helps with this board\"); the client's Care Team rows say \"works without an AI assistant here\" for caregivers who de-selected concierge. Both ride `careConsent()` → the two-party resolver.\n  - **Space scope CLOSED same day** (founder: \"close that open piece\"). The member's per-space de-selection (\"AI for me in WAG, but not Melanie's group\") writes `scope_type='space'` rows from a second group in the Privacy list — your own memberships, one column, each showing \"has switched its own AI off\" (disabled) when the SPACE chose that (mutual visibility again). Enforced where a space context actually exists today: `claude-chat` skips a space-kind chat when the space's `assistant_enabled=false` (the space's own switch finally means something server-side, not just a hidden brain) OR the sender holds a space de-selection row for it; `assistant-search` takes `space_ids` (criteria.spaceScope, uuid-validated) and steps aside when the caller de-selected any of them or any has `assistant_enabled=false`; `ContributionsFeed`'s brain on a space page also reads `consentOn('space', spaceId)`. ⚠ `AssistantConsentList`'s membership read filters `eq('profile_id', me)` — space_members RLS shows fellow members, so an unfiltered read lists spaces via other people's rows.\n  - **Still open**: `assistant-brief`/`assistant-feed` have no per-space context to check (sections span all spaces of a kind; threads are the member's own) — the full per-entity AI Partner fabric is where those become space-scoped; `aspect` scope reserved; onboarding's AI-consent step (the sequenced dependency is satisfied — the table exists, onboarding can write to it directly).\n\n- **Assistant actions — Claude editing a member's own page** (founder 2026-08-11; BUILT 2026-08-13): the Claude Code loop on-platform. `profiles.assistant_can_edit` (default **false** — a hand that writes is opted into, never inherited) switches it on in Profile → Privacy; the tools arm only in the **profile** thread, so an ask from Marketplace gets pointed here instead of quietly rewriting the page from the wrong room. Six operations, all scoped server-side to the trigger's `profile_id` (no tool takes a target): tagline, home summary, story, one contact field, add/remove categories — an empty value CLEARS, which is what makes \"put it back\" work when the field started empty. Bounded tool loop (4 rounds, then `tool_choice: none` forces the report); one `assistant_queries` row per exchange with usage summed, so a multi-turn edit doesn't burn the cap faster than a conversation; a write with no report falls back to a generated summary. The 141-name category vocabulary rides in the system block so a category can only ever be one that exists. Context card at the top of the thread is a receipt of Claude's OWN inputs, and `?ask=` prefills the composer unsent. Step 4 landed too: the Profile thread's \"Your page\" toggle now embeds the REAL page (`/members/:id?preview=1&embed=1`) rather than opening a tab — `?embed=1` stands the app chrome down (App.tsx's `isEmbed`) and hides the self view-toggle, so the frame reads as the page and not a second app. It's sticky at ≥1024px so it stays in view while the conversation scrolls under it, and Claude speaking in the profile thread bumps `pageNonce`, so an edit appears without anyone pressing refresh. Below 1024px a whole page in a frame teaches nobody anything — that width gets the new-tab door and says why. Spec + the consent boundary: [`docs/ASSISTANT_ACTIONS.md`](docs/ASSISTANT_ACTIONS.md).\n- **Side-by-side \"Your page\" in the assistant's Profile management thread** (founder 2026-08-11, unfinished): the toggle currently opens the public page in a NEW TAB. The embedded version was built and reverted — the iframe collapsed to 2×2 even with inline `width:100%; height:60vh; display:block` (the style attribute was confirmed present on the element, so something outside it is winning). Worth one pass with real devtools; the goal is page-beside-conversation, the way a Claude Code session works.\n\n## Housekeeping\n- Downloads folder has accumulated many `lichen-*` zip duplicates from the old manual deploy flow — irrelevant to the repo, but the source-of-truth is always `main` on GitHub.\n- There may be stray leftover files under `src/data/` (old zips, nested dirs) from earlier bad copies — safe to clean up if found.\n\n===== docs/ASSISTANT_ACTIONS.md — What an assistant may and may not do on a member’s behalf. =====\n\n# Assistant actions — letting Claude edit a member's own page\n\n**Status:** BUILT 2026-08-13 — all four steps of the build order below. Live behind `profiles.assistant_can_edit`,\ndefault off, switched on in Profile → Privacy → \"What the assistant may change\",\nand armed only in the Profile thread. One correction from testing: an empty\nvalue CLEARS a field rather than erroring — without that, \"put it back\" could\nnever undo a write onto something that started empty, which is most first\nedits. Founder 2026-08-11: \"it should load a chat\nwith Claude that shows the user the context Claude already has on the\nsubject, with the opportunity to add more before pressing send… then Claude\nlets you know when they're done so you can review it live and continue to\nmake dialogue-based edits.\"\n\nThis is the Claude Code loop, on-platform, scoped to a member's own\nsubsection. Today the assistant can only *talk*: Snapshot hands over a\nproposal to confirm, the Home summary button writes into a text box. Nothing\nlets Claude say \"done — I rewrote your tagline,\" because it has no way to\nwrite. This closes that.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. **Context card** — opening the Profile management thread, Claude leads\n   with a receipt of what it's working from: current tagline, story length,\n   categories picked, which contact fields are filled and which are empty.\n   Not a description of the member — a statement of its own inputs, so\n   there's no mystery about what it knows.\n2. **Editable ask** — the door's intent lands in the composer (the existing\n   `?ask=` prefill), unsent, so \"write my home summary\" can become \"…and keep\n   it under 100 words, mention the pasture\" before it goes.\n3. **Action** — Claude calls one of the allowed operations below.\n4. **Report** — it says plainly what changed and what it left alone.\n5. **Review and iterate** — the member looks at the page and says \"warmer\",\n   \"too long\", and it goes again.\n\n## The allowed operations (the whole list)\n\nAnthropic tool-use in `assistant-feed`. The assistant may call ONLY these,\nand only against the caller's own profile (`profile_id` from the trigger —\nnever an id the model supplies):\n\n| tool | writes | notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `set_tagline` | `profiles.page.tagline` | ≤ 90 chars |\n| `set_home_summary` | `profiles.page.homeSummary` | the Home welcome |\n| `set_story` | `profiles.page.story` | full replace; keep the old value in the report so it can be undone by asking |\n| `set_contact_field` | `profiles.contact.<field>` | field must be one of ContactFields' keys |\n| `add_categories` / `remove_categories` | `profile_categories` | ids must exist in `categories`; capabilities follow, as `applySnapshot` already does |\n\nDeliberately NOT in v1: publishing the page, posting to the feed, anything\ntouching other members, anything in `space_*`. Those are consequential in a\nway that wants a confirm step, not a chat message.\n\n## Boundary rules\n\n- **Own profile only.** The service-role client already knows who triggered\n  the row; the model never supplies a target.\n- **A member switch.** \"Let Claude edit my page directly\" in Profile →\n  Privacy, default OFF for now. With it off, the assistant proposes in prose\n  and the member applies by hand — exactly today's behavior.\n- **Every write is announced.** No silent edits: the reply must name what\n  changed. A write with no report is a bug.\n- **Reversible by conversation.** The report carries the previous value so\n  \"put it back\" works without an undo stack.\n- **Public-page fields only.** Nothing here can reach `financial_positions`,\n  location, care, or anything else private — those aren't in the table above\n  and must not be added without their own consent conversation.\n\n## Build order\n\n1. Tool definitions + the allowed-ops executor in `assistant-feed`, behind\n   the (default-off) member switch.\n2. The context card at the top of the Profile management thread.\n3. Point \"Fill out with Claude\" / \"Have Claude write this from the full\n   story\" at the thread with an editable prefill instead of acting directly.\n4. Live review: the side-by-side page view. DONE — the 2×2 collapse didn't\n   reproduce once the frame carried an explicit `display: block` and\n   `.afeed__page` `align-self: stretch` (it's a flex item of a flex column,\n   which is how it failed to stretch the first time). The frame loads the\n   real page with `?embed=1`, which stands the app chrome down so it doesn't\n   render a second app inside itself; it's sticky from 1024px up, and\n   Claude's reply in this thread reloads it, so an edit is something you\n   watch rather than something you're told about.\n\n## Watch out\n\n- Parse EVERY text block of the Anthropic reply, not `content[0].text` —\n  a non-text leading block silently produced an empty result in\n  `profile-snapshot` (fixed there, same trap here).\n- Tool calls and the daily cap (`ASSISTANT_FEED_CAP`) interact: a multi-turn\n  edit shouldn't burn the cap faster than a conversation. Count a completed\n  exchange, not each tool round-trip.\n\n## Read-only lookups in the help room (2026-08-16)\n\nThe doctrine tells the assistant how Lichen works; these tell it how THIS\nmember's Lichen is actually set up, so \"why can't people book me?\" is\nanswered from data instead of inference.\n\n- `my_setup` — the asking member's handle, public page, findability,\n  pronouns, timezone, availability windows by kind, booking types, membership.\n- `my_spaces` — the spaces they belong to and whether they steward each.\n\nSame safety shape as the edit tools, and for the same reason: **neither tool\ntakes a target.** Both have an empty input schema and are run against the\nprofile that sent the triggering message. A member who says \"I'm an admin,\nlook up someone else\" cannot be complied with, because there is no argument\nto fill — verified live, and the refusal was structural rather than\nmerely well-behaved.\n\nRead-only: nothing here writes.";
